1
00:00:02,029 --> 00:00:04,102
[tense music]

2
00:00:55,819 --> 00:00:59,014
[engine revving]

3
00:01:09,261 --> 00:01:11,334
[metal crashes]

4
00:01:21,538 --> 00:01:24,039
[indistinct chatter]

5
00:01:29,688 --> 00:01:33,092
[faint thumping]

6
00:01:36,929 --> 00:01:40,957
[man speaking indistinctly]

7
00:01:41,865 --> 00:01:43,531
[keys jingling]

8
00:01:47,364 --> 00:01:48,371
[clicks]

9
00:01:57,381 --> 00:01:58,414
[man over earpiece]
<i>He's coming down.</i>

10
00:01:59,719 --> 00:02:00,980
[telephone ringing]

11
00:02:01,082 --> 00:02:03,914
[gate opening]

12
00:02:04,724 --> 00:02:08,083
[indistinct chatter]

13
00:02:13,833 --> 00:02:14,958
[elevator bell dings]

14
00:02:20,273 --> 00:02:23,466
Well, I wanted to reassure
you and your father,

15
00:02:23,568 --> 00:02:24,605
you're in good hands.

16
00:02:25,744 --> 00:02:27,075
Ambitious...

17
00:02:27,178 --> 00:02:29,144
- How'd it go?
- Almost done.

18
00:02:29,246 --> 00:02:30,941
[businessman
speaks indistinctly]

19
00:02:41,353 --> 00:02:42,623
All this...

20
00:02:44,257 --> 00:02:45,595
began with that.

21
00:02:46,498 --> 00:02:48,992
We're gonna take great care
of your company, sir.

22
00:02:50,769 --> 00:02:51,863
I know you will.

23
00:02:55,041 --> 00:02:58,804
[businessman
speaks indistinctly]

24
00:02:59,811 --> 00:03:01,210
[car honks]

25
00:03:01,312 --> 00:03:02,839
[businessman]
All right, gentlemen.

26
00:03:02,942 --> 00:03:04,845
See you in a week
when we make it official.

27
00:03:04,948 --> 00:03:06,449
Great day.

28
00:03:06,983 --> 00:03:08,143
[car door opens]

29
00:03:11,824 --> 00:03:12,785
[car door closes]

30
00:03:14,056 --> 00:03:15,220
Congrats.

31
00:03:15,322 --> 00:03:16,393
Thank you, brother.

32
00:03:36,649 --> 00:03:38,578
Relax.

33
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:41,112
This is what you wanted.
You should be happy.

34
00:03:41,214 --> 00:03:42,320
I am.

35
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:44,421
Are you?

36
00:03:46,859 --> 00:03:48,359
For me, it's, uh...

37
00:03:49,586 --> 00:03:50,724
bittersweet.

38
00:03:57,066 --> 00:03:59,931
[soft music]

39
00:04:24,187 --> 00:04:25,528
- [Tibu] Thank you.
- [staff speaks Thai]

40
00:04:33,430 --> 00:04:34,864
[Tibu in English] Do what
you need to do, then come over

41
00:04:34,966 --> 00:04:36,641
so we can settle
our business, yeah?

42
00:04:36,743 --> 00:04:37,969
[Cole] Sure.

43
00:04:54,084 --> 00:04:56,460
- [Cole] All good?
- Yeah, all good.

44
00:04:58,123 --> 00:05:00,358
Oh, and, boss, uh,
tomorrow night's guest list

45
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:01,557
just came through.

46
00:05:01,659 --> 00:05:02,791
It's on your tablet.

47
00:05:02,893 --> 00:05:04,567
[Cole] Thanks. I'll take a look.

48
00:05:05,662 --> 00:05:06,734
[door opens]

49
00:05:13,411 --> 00:05:15,512
How did you become
so good at this?

50
00:05:17,010 --> 00:05:21,144
When I was a rookie,
they had me work the jail.

51
00:05:23,423 --> 00:05:26,490
Best chess players in the world
live behind bars.

52
00:05:27,418 --> 00:05:28,360
Mm.

53
00:05:30,427 --> 00:05:32,188
Do you miss
being a police officer?

54
00:05:32,932 --> 00:05:34,432
I miss the action.

55
00:05:35,836 --> 00:05:37,200
Not the politics.

56
00:05:37,302 --> 00:05:38,535
- [chess piece thuds]
- Check.

57
00:05:40,997 --> 00:05:42,440
[Tibu] You can never go back?

58
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,502
[Cole] No.

59
00:05:44,604 --> 00:05:45,938
I made some mistakes.

60
00:05:46,970 --> 00:05:49,209
Pissed off the wrong people.

61
00:05:49,311 --> 00:05:50,382
[inhales sharply]

62
00:05:51,510 --> 00:05:53,011
Today, um...

63
00:05:55,013 --> 00:05:56,346
would have been
your father's birthday.

64
00:05:56,449 --> 00:05:57,719
[chuckles]

65
00:05:59,116 --> 00:06:00,925
Trying to break
my concentration.

66
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:02,394
Whatever it takes to win.

67
00:06:03,793 --> 00:06:05,520
Well, you'll need
all the help you can get.

68
00:06:05,623 --> 00:06:07,124
[chuckles]

69
00:06:12,839 --> 00:06:13,900
You're okay?

70
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:18,003
Yeah.

71
00:06:20,376 --> 00:06:21,408
Thanks for remembering.

72
00:06:21,510 --> 00:06:24,412
Oh. I wish I could have met him.

73
00:06:24,514 --> 00:06:25,912
[Cole] Yeah, you'd have
loved him.

74
00:06:27,084 --> 00:06:28,585
He was, uh...

75
00:06:31,750 --> 00:06:33,216
I mean, he could play.

76
00:06:34,526 --> 00:06:35,885
He'd have kicked your ass
worse than I do.

77
00:06:35,987 --> 00:06:38,727
- [chuckles]
- And taken your money.

78
00:06:40,096 --> 00:06:41,490
Check.

79
00:06:41,593 --> 00:06:42,896
[exhales]

80
00:06:45,932 --> 00:06:48,836
If you were me,
what would you do?

81
00:06:50,208 --> 00:06:51,707
I'd probably surrender.

82
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:54,306
Ahh.

83
00:06:54,408 --> 00:06:56,712
[Tibu laughing]

84
00:06:57,744 --> 00:06:59,982
- But you don't have to.
- Ah.

85
00:07:00,084 --> 00:07:01,247
No, you've won.

86
00:07:01,349 --> 00:07:02,916
[both chuckle]

87
00:07:07,619 --> 00:07:09,519
[gulps, inhales]

88
00:07:09,621 --> 00:07:10,627
[smacks lips]

89
00:07:21,436 --> 00:07:22,474
[chuckles softly]

90
00:07:27,704 --> 00:07:29,206
[sighs]

91
00:07:31,544 --> 00:07:33,815
[clears throat]

92
00:07:38,882 --> 00:07:40,316
Happy birthday, Dad.

93
00:07:46,966 --> 00:07:49,094
[birds chirping]

94
00:08:03,313 --> 00:08:04,747
[staff speaks Thai]

95
00:08:04,849 --> 00:08:05,841
[Kameron in English] The dinner
precedes cake cutting.

96
00:08:05,943 --> 00:08:06,876
Ready for your big night?

97
00:08:06,978 --> 00:08:08,309
My father's gonna make a speech.

98
00:08:08,412 --> 00:08:09,917
- You know how much I hate this.
- [both chuckle]

99
00:08:12,519 --> 00:08:13,715
[engine starts]

100
00:08:13,817 --> 00:08:14,988
[speaks Thai]

101
00:08:22,263 --> 00:08:24,569
[in English] Yeah. Yeah, yeah.
Yes, well, it was like, um,

102
00:08:24,671 --> 00:08:26,500
what is-- what is this language
you've been learning?

103
00:08:26,602 --> 00:08:28,240
I don't-- I don't recognize it.

104
00:08:28,342 --> 00:08:29,805
Are you sure
you've been learning?

105
00:08:30,835 --> 00:08:32,643
[muffled laughter]

106
00:08:33,474 --> 00:08:35,341
[speaking Thai]

107
00:08:35,443 --> 00:08:37,945
[all exclaim]

108
00:08:39,813 --> 00:08:41,784
[speaking Thai indistinctly]

109
00:08:44,014 --> 00:08:46,558
[chattering, laughing]

110
00:08:54,891 --> 00:08:56,733
[tapping glass]

111
00:08:57,901 --> 00:08:59,432
[in English] I have.
I have, yeah. I went last year.

112
00:08:59,534 --> 00:09:00,532
[Tibu clears throat]

113
00:09:00,634 --> 00:09:02,571
[breathes deeply]

114
00:09:02,673 --> 00:09:05,575
You spend your life
chasing success,

115
00:09:05,677 --> 00:09:08,607
only to one day realize
that all that matters

116
00:09:08,709 --> 00:09:10,708
is how you achieved it.

117
00:09:10,810 --> 00:09:12,210
What you've left behind.

118
00:09:13,586 --> 00:09:16,280
- Ours is a very dirty business.
- Who's that?

119
00:09:16,382 --> 00:09:19,622
[Tibu] But our company's
"ethics over profits" spirit...

120
00:09:19,725 --> 00:09:22,451
[Taran] Jaran Daniles.
Trans-Pacific Exports.

121
00:09:22,553 --> 00:09:26,398
Cleanest record on the high seas
over the past 40 years,

122
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:29,664
and that... is what
I am most proud of.

123
00:09:29,766 --> 00:09:32,002
- [guest 1] Yes.
- [guests clapping]

124
00:09:32,104 --> 00:09:33,429
[guest 2] Bravo.

125
00:09:36,775 --> 00:09:38,401
[Tibu] I'd like to thank you
for joining me...

126
00:09:38,503 --> 00:09:39,836
- [man] Yes. Good to meet you.
- ...and my son Kameron

127
00:09:39,938 --> 00:09:41,672
on this special occasion.

128
00:09:41,774 --> 00:09:43,272
[man] El Salvador.

129
00:09:43,374 --> 00:09:45,149
[Tibu] Tonight, we celebrate
a new chapter

130
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:46,984
for the Campallo family.

131
00:09:47,086 --> 00:09:48,411
A new beginning.

132
00:09:49,389 --> 00:09:51,188
I'm so proud
of the work Kameron did

133
00:09:51,290 --> 00:09:52,587
to grow the business,

134
00:09:52,689 --> 00:09:55,425
to help make this sale
a reality.

135
00:09:55,527 --> 00:09:56,490
Without his efforts,
none of this

136
00:09:56,592 --> 00:09:58,295
would have been possible.

137
00:09:58,397 --> 00:10:00,423
And we did it the right way.

138
00:10:01,969 --> 00:10:02,931
Together.

139
00:10:04,399 --> 00:10:05,797
Come.

140
00:10:05,899 --> 00:10:07,936
[guests clapping and cheering]

141
00:10:13,037 --> 00:10:15,240
[guests cheering loudly]

142
00:10:23,421 --> 00:10:25,218
Now, we toast and drink.

143
00:10:25,653 --> 00:10:28,154
[cheering continues]

144
00:10:30,429 --> 00:10:31,927
[Tibu] To celebrate this day.

145
00:10:36,664 --> 00:10:38,164
The one you wanted.

146
00:10:39,402 --> 00:10:40,833
Thank you.

147
00:10:40,935 --> 00:10:42,172
- Thank you.
- [guests clapping]

148
00:10:42,274 --> 00:10:43,906
Cole, where are you?

149
00:10:45,773 --> 00:10:47,745
Come. Join the family.

150
00:10:56,154 --> 00:10:57,282
Open it.

151
00:11:00,986 --> 00:11:02,359
Kameron likes the flash,

152
00:11:02,461 --> 00:11:03,858
but, uh, we prefer this, right?

153
00:11:03,961 --> 00:11:06,830
This is a watch
for a man of action. [chuckles]

154
00:11:07,864 --> 00:11:09,426
- Uh, read the back.
- [box thuds]

155
00:11:12,504 --> 00:11:13,969
What does the inscription say?

156
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:15,938
It's a date.

157
00:11:16,970 --> 00:11:19,005
It's the day he saved my life.

158
00:11:19,108 --> 00:11:23,037
Five years ago,
he risked his life to save mine.

159
00:11:23,139 --> 00:11:24,683
I offered him a job,

160
00:11:25,484 --> 00:11:27,415
and he has since become family.

161
00:11:27,517 --> 00:11:29,644
[guests clapping]

162
00:11:32,015 --> 00:11:33,082
Thanks, Tibu.

163
00:11:33,184 --> 00:11:35,287
[Tibu] Thank you. Thank you.

164
00:11:37,894 --> 00:11:40,393
- To family.
- [guests] To family!

165
00:11:40,496 --> 00:11:42,899
[cheering]

166
00:11:43,962 --> 00:11:45,267
They're celebrating.

167
00:11:45,369 --> 00:11:46,463
But don't worry.

168
00:11:47,671 --> 00:11:49,400
The sale will be dead tonight.

169
00:11:56,339 --> 00:11:58,048
Wasn't so bad, now, was it?

170
00:11:58,151 --> 00:11:59,712
[chuckles]

171
00:11:59,814 --> 00:12:01,148
It was a wonderful night.

172
00:12:04,047 --> 00:12:05,350
Everything okay?

173
00:12:06,224 --> 00:12:07,319
Yeah.

174
00:12:08,753 --> 00:12:12,390
I just, uh, never imagined
I would ever sell the company.

175
00:12:13,397 --> 00:12:14,557
Never wanted to.

176
00:12:17,370 --> 00:12:18,594
Then why'd you do it?

177
00:12:25,708 --> 00:12:27,075
I did it for Kameron.

178
00:12:28,005 --> 00:12:29,671
KMG was, uh...

179
00:12:30,943 --> 00:12:32,478
my dream, not his.

180
00:12:33,181 --> 00:12:36,348
The shipping business
is, uh, not for him.

181
00:12:39,123 --> 00:12:41,892
I wanted to give him the chance
to chase his own dreams.

182
00:12:44,761 --> 00:12:46,457
He'll never forget it, Tibu.

183
00:12:49,763 --> 00:12:50,868
Thank you.

184
00:12:53,934 --> 00:12:55,367
Why are we going this way?

185
00:12:58,367 --> 00:13:00,537
Looks like a road closure.

186
00:13:16,990 --> 00:13:18,187
[policeman 1 speaks Thai]

187
00:13:18,289 --> 00:13:20,227
[policeman 2 speaking Thai]

188
00:13:24,902 --> 00:13:26,536
[in English] I'll back us
out of here.

189
00:13:26,638 --> 00:13:30,072
[policeman 1 speaking Thai]

190
00:13:32,571 --> 00:13:34,076
- [brake squeals]
- [policeman 2 speaking Thai]

191
00:13:36,448 --> 00:13:37,513
[exclaims in Thai]

192
00:13:37,615 --> 00:13:38,580
[in English] What is this?

193
00:13:38,682 --> 00:13:39,774
[policeman 1 speaks Thai]

194
00:13:41,444 --> 00:13:43,045
[policeman 2 speaking Thai]

195
00:13:43,147 --> 00:13:44,185
[exclaims in Thai]

196
00:13:53,589 --> 00:13:54,659
- [in English] Get down!
- [gunshots]

197
00:13:54,761 --> 00:13:56,334
[yelps]

198
00:13:56,436 --> 00:13:57,792
[hitman] Take 'em down!

199
00:14:00,834 --> 00:14:02,038
[engine revving]

200
00:14:05,271 --> 00:14:06,768
- [gunshots]
- [tires screech]

201
00:14:08,714 --> 00:14:10,849
- [grunts]
- [car alarm wailing]

202
00:14:11,546 --> 00:14:12,543
Ahh!

203
00:14:14,183 --> 00:14:15,887
- [gunshots]
- [hitman] Shoot the tires!

204
00:14:18,218 --> 00:14:19,849
- [car engine whirring]
- You okay?

205
00:14:19,952 --> 00:14:21,321
I'm okay.

206
00:14:27,162 --> 00:14:30,931
- [engine revving]
- [tires screeching]

207
00:14:31,033 --> 00:14:34,070
- [gunman yelling in pain]
- Ah!

208
00:14:35,970 --> 00:14:39,009
[Tibu breathing shakily]

209
00:14:41,871 --> 00:14:44,014
- [Cole] Ah, shit.
- [distant police siren wailing]

210
00:14:44,913 --> 00:14:47,045
[Tibu] What just happened?

211
00:14:47,147 --> 00:14:48,579
[shakily] Those were police.

212
00:14:51,655 --> 00:14:54,118
[shallow breathing]

213
00:14:54,220 --> 00:14:55,954
- Please...
- [Cole sighs]

214
00:14:56,056 --> 00:14:57,952
Please look after Kameron.

215
00:14:58,488 --> 00:15:01,622
[labored breathing] Look at me.

216
00:15:01,724 --> 00:15:03,996
If-- if I don't make it,
I can't help him.

217
00:15:04,098 --> 00:15:06,271
Nothing will happen to Kameron.

218
00:15:06,873 --> 00:15:09,130
- [gasping rapidly]
- Stay with me, Tibu.

219
00:15:09,232 --> 00:15:10,398
Stay with me.

220
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:12,804
[continues gasping rapidly]

221
00:15:12,906 --> 00:15:13,868
[gasping stops]

222
00:15:17,945 --> 00:15:20,842
[emotional music]

223
00:15:34,962 --> 00:15:36,396
[cell phone rings]

224
00:15:37,930 --> 00:15:38,865
Yeah?

225
00:15:38,967 --> 00:15:40,130
[Cole over phone]<i> Taran,</i>

226
00:15:40,232 --> 00:15:41,673
<i>is Kameron with you?</i>

227
00:15:42,142 --> 00:15:44,640
[Taran] Yeah. I've got eyes
on him. He's just got back.

228
00:15:44,742 --> 00:15:47,509
Listen, we were ambushed.

229
00:15:47,611 --> 00:15:48,903
Tibu's dead.

230
00:15:50,416 --> 00:15:51,477
The fuck?

231
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:54,881
Did you call the police?

232
00:15:54,983 --> 00:15:56,652
<i>The police are involved.</i>

233
00:15:56,754 --> 00:15:58,418
We can't trust anybody.

234
00:16:01,317 --> 00:16:02,818
[zipper unzips]

235
00:16:05,225 --> 00:16:06,990
One of these guys was American.

236
00:16:07,092 --> 00:16:08,558
<i>US passport.</i>

237
00:16:08,660 --> 00:16:11,167
-<i> 6573247. Run it.</i>
- [cell phone thuds]

238
00:16:12,338 --> 00:16:14,229
3247.

239
00:16:14,331 --> 00:16:15,633
Checking. Stand by.

240
00:16:16,742 --> 00:16:19,004
I've got him. Jonathan Rogers.

241
00:16:19,106 --> 00:16:20,935
Former marine. MARSOC.

242
00:16:22,275 --> 00:16:24,246
Rogers is a crewman for the KMG.

243
00:16:24,913 --> 00:16:26,542
<i>He works for us.</i>

244
00:16:26,644 --> 00:16:28,819
He's departing
on the Artemis tonight.

245
00:16:28,921 --> 00:16:30,582
It's gonna leave port
in two hours.

246
00:16:31,623 --> 00:16:32,749
<i>What's your plan?</i>

247
00:16:33,693 --> 00:16:35,092
[Cole] I'm headed to the port.

248
00:16:36,355 --> 00:16:37,820
I'll find out who did this.

249
00:16:41,361 --> 00:16:43,529
[indistinct chattering
on tablet]

250
00:16:44,835 --> 00:16:46,433
Campallo is dead, sir.

251
00:16:47,637 --> 00:16:48,666
Good.

252
00:16:50,775 --> 00:16:53,335
So, what do you want?

253
00:16:53,437 --> 00:16:54,804
We have a problem, sir.

254
00:16:56,110 --> 00:16:57,477
His bodyguard got away.

255
00:17:04,781 --> 00:17:06,684
Tell the police
to put out an APB.

256
00:17:08,155 --> 00:17:10,193
But... one more thing.

257
00:17:12,126 --> 00:17:13,823
Don't bring him in alive.

258
00:17:19,701 --> 00:17:21,631
[reporter on TV]<i> Two police</i>
<i>officers were murdered tonight</i>

259
00:17:21,733 --> 00:17:24,273
<i>while performing</i>
<i>a routine traffic stop.</i>

260
00:17:24,375 --> 00:17:27,769
<i>Billionaire shipping tycoon</i>
<i>Manuel Tibu Campallo</i>

261
00:17:27,871 --> 00:17:29,814
-<i> was also killed.</i>
- [gift wrapper rustles]

262
00:17:29,916 --> 00:17:32,109
<i>The suspect</i>
<i>is a British citizen</i>

263
00:17:32,211 --> 00:17:33,611
<i>named Cole Reed.</i>

264
00:17:33,713 --> 00:17:36,881
<i>Reed worked as</i>
<i>Campallo's personal bodyguard.</i>

265
00:17:37,851 --> 00:17:41,620
<i>The suspect is very dangerous</i>
<i>and still on the loose.</i>

266
00:17:41,722 --> 00:17:44,625
<i>A citywide order to shelter</i>
<i>is in place until--</i>

267
00:17:44,728 --> 00:17:46,420
[buzzing]

268
00:17:46,522 --> 00:17:50,826
[continues buzzing]

269
00:17:50,928 --> 00:17:52,463
- This is Ellis.
- [man over phone]<i> Miss Ellis,</i>

270
00:17:52,565 --> 00:17:54,098
<i>we need you</i>
<i>to report immediately.</i>

271
00:17:54,734 --> 00:17:57,234
- Well, I, um--
-<i> The Artemis is short crew.</i>

272
00:17:57,336 --> 00:17:58,741
<i>Departs at midnight.</i>

273
00:17:58,843 --> 00:17:59,969
<i>We need you there now.</i>

274
00:18:00,872 --> 00:18:03,443
Sir, I just got in
from the Venus San Diego haul,

275
00:18:03,545 --> 00:18:06,816
24 days across, and my flight,
well, it's in, uh,

276
00:18:06,918 --> 00:18:08,014
my flight home's in three hours.

277
00:18:08,116 --> 00:18:09,114
<i>Miss Ellis, you're still</i>

278
00:18:09,216 --> 00:18:11,022
<i>a probationary employee.</i>

279
00:18:11,124 --> 00:18:14,221
Sir, I-I have my daughter
this weekend in LA.

280
00:18:14,323 --> 00:18:16,452
<i>Listen, if you're not</i>
<i>at your post</i>

281
00:18:16,554 --> 00:18:18,256
<i>on the Artemis in an hour,</i>

282
00:18:18,358 --> 00:18:20,122
<i>KMG's gonna have to let you go.</i>

283
00:18:20,224 --> 00:18:21,396
[scoffs]

284
00:18:22,030 --> 00:18:24,135
Okay. Roger that.

285
00:18:25,768 --> 00:18:26,797
Fuck.

286
00:18:27,407 --> 00:18:28,436
Fuck.

287
00:18:29,598 --> 00:18:30,966
[exhales] Oh, fuck.

288
00:18:40,918 --> 00:18:42,483
[Cole exhales sharply]

289
00:18:59,099 --> 00:19:01,671
[keypad beeping]

290
00:19:01,773 --> 00:19:04,802
[beeping continues]

291
00:19:06,437 --> 00:19:09,477
[door opens, closes]

292
00:19:11,742 --> 00:19:14,075
Kameron,
Detective Jamai is here.

293
00:19:15,782 --> 00:19:17,249
- [Kameron] Evening, Detective.
- Good evening.

294
00:19:17,351 --> 00:19:18,687
[Kameron] Evening, Officer.

295
00:19:18,789 --> 00:19:19,753
My condolences.

296
00:19:19,856 --> 00:19:20,857
Thank you.

297
00:19:20,959 --> 00:19:22,718
I am sorry, but we are going

298
00:19:22,820 --> 00:19:24,425
to have to ask you
a few questions.

299
00:19:24,527 --> 00:19:26,597
- [sniffles] Of course. Ah...
- [phone buzzes]

300
00:19:26,699 --> 00:19:28,098
[continues buzzing]

301
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:29,559
Uh, Taran, could you pour
these gentlemen

302
00:19:29,661 --> 00:19:31,096
- a drink, please?
- Of course.

303
00:19:31,198 --> 00:19:33,232
Hello? Who is this?

304
00:19:33,335 --> 00:19:34,799
[over phone]<i> Kameron, it's Cole.</i>

305
00:19:36,608 --> 00:19:37,538
<i>Listen.</i>

306
00:19:39,437 --> 00:19:40,706
Your father, uh...

307
00:19:43,616 --> 00:19:44,545
[inhales]

308
00:19:46,014 --> 00:19:47,218
I'm so sorry.

309
00:19:48,148 --> 00:19:49,484
[sighs] I tried.

310
00:19:51,013 --> 00:19:53,288
The police are here
asking questions.

311
00:19:53,390 --> 00:19:55,122
On the news,
they're saying you killed him.

312
00:19:55,224 --> 00:19:56,689
<i>That's not what happened.</i>

313
00:19:58,225 --> 00:19:59,362
<i>We were ambushed.</i>

314
00:20:00,394 --> 00:20:01,795
You need to stay locked down.

315
00:20:02,664 --> 00:20:05,632
Whoever killed Tibu
will be coming for you next.

316
00:20:11,172 --> 00:20:12,370
[exhales, sniffles]

317
00:20:12,472 --> 00:20:14,674
[police siren wails in distance]

318
00:20:22,050 --> 00:20:23,144
[phone thuds]

319
00:20:31,029 --> 00:20:32,423
[port guard 1 speaking Thai]

320
00:20:32,526 --> 00:20:34,991
[indistinct announcement
over PA]

321
00:20:42,235 --> 00:20:43,505
[siren wails]

322
00:20:45,834 --> 00:20:48,708
[speaking Thai over radio]

323
00:20:52,248 --> 00:20:56,078
[port security speaking in Thai]

324
00:20:57,184 --> 00:20:59,719
[tense music]

325
00:21:03,193 --> 00:21:05,527
[port guard 2 speaking Thai]

326
00:21:10,869 --> 00:21:12,259
[keyboard clacks]

327
00:21:13,396 --> 00:21:14,935
[port guard 1 in English]
Make your way through security

328
00:21:15,037 --> 00:21:16,131
on your right.

329
00:21:18,472 --> 00:21:21,642
[port worker 1 speaks Thai]

330
00:21:30,449 --> 00:21:34,523
[indistinct chatter]

331
00:21:35,126 --> 00:21:36,657
[port worker 2 speaks Thai]

332
00:21:59,818 --> 00:22:00,846
