340
00:22:33,915 --> 00:22:35,583
[reporter on TV]<i> For more</i>
<i>on this developing story,</i>

341
00:22:35,685 --> 00:22:38,079
<i>we go live to Stan Beckwith</i>
<i>on the scene.</i>

342
00:22:38,181 --> 00:22:40,015
[Stan]<i> New details</i>
<i>are emerging tonight</i>

343
00:22:40,118 --> 00:22:42,424
<i>following a shooting</i>
<i>in downtown Bangkok.</i>

344
00:22:42,526 --> 00:22:43,960
<i>Sources say</i>
<i>the incident may have been</i>

345
00:22:44,062 --> 00:22:45,224
<i>an attempted kidnapping</i>

346
00:22:45,326 --> 00:22:46,963
<i>targeting KMG CEO</i>

347
00:22:47,065 --> 00:22:48,960
<i>Manuel Tibu Campallo,</i>

348
00:22:49,062 --> 00:22:51,295
<i>allegedly carried out</i>
<i>by his longtime bodyguard,</i>

349
00:22:51,397 --> 00:22:52,596
<i>Cole Reed.</i>

350
00:22:52,698 --> 00:22:54,068
<i>Campallo was pronounced dead</i>

351
00:22:54,170 --> 00:22:55,234
<i>at the scene.</i>

352
00:22:55,336 --> 00:22:56,297
Captain. [knocks]

353
00:22:57,876 --> 00:22:58,970
You may enter.

354
00:23:00,039 --> 00:23:03,440
- Is everybody on board?
- Yes, sir. We're good.

355
00:23:04,143 --> 00:23:05,983
Who are you, and what are you
doing on my bridge?

356
00:23:06,085 --> 00:23:07,808
[Mateo] New third mate, Captain.

357
00:23:07,910 --> 00:23:08,909
I don't need a third mate.

358
00:23:09,011 --> 00:23:10,881
I have 20 good men on board.

359
00:23:10,984 --> 00:23:12,486
Well, Captain,
I didn't wanna be here either,

360
00:23:12,588 --> 00:23:14,782
but, uh, company asked me
to report.

361
00:23:14,884 --> 00:23:15,957
Rama called in sick, sir.

362
00:23:16,059 --> 00:23:17,351
KMG sent her.

363
00:23:19,756 --> 00:23:21,025
[exhales sharply]

364
00:23:23,666 --> 00:23:26,767
[smacks lips]
Would you like me to twirl, sir?

365
00:23:29,437 --> 00:23:30,931
I'm not a fan of attitude.

366
00:23:31,033 --> 00:23:33,268
Oh, no, neither am I. At all.

367
00:23:35,905 --> 00:23:38,449
[paper rustles softly]

368
00:23:40,914 --> 00:23:44,012
Well, if the company,
in all its genius,

369
00:23:44,114 --> 00:23:46,523
wants you here,
then welcome on board.

370
00:23:47,425 --> 00:23:48,855
[Angie] I like
your necklace, sir.

371
00:23:51,890 --> 00:23:53,497
- You know what it is?
- I do.

372
00:23:53,599 --> 00:23:56,434
That is a Viking symbol
of guidance and protection.

373
00:23:59,939 --> 00:24:01,769
Impressive. Theo.

374
00:24:02,870 --> 00:24:04,203
Can you take the young lady
to her cabin?

375
00:24:04,305 --> 00:24:05,366
[Theo] Sir.

376
00:24:06,242 --> 00:24:07,269
[Angie] Thank you.

377
00:24:09,112 --> 00:24:10,140
You're welcome.

378
00:24:15,944 --> 00:24:17,186
Anything else, sir?

379
00:24:17,722 --> 00:24:20,385
[Marko sighs] The two of you
are on the night shift.

380
00:24:20,487 --> 00:24:21,723
Keep an eye on her.

381
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:31,667
[tense music]

382
00:25:08,303 --> 00:25:10,640
[horn blaring]

383
00:25:14,371 --> 00:25:16,778
- Hard to starboard!
- [Theo] Hard to starboard.

384
00:25:18,612 --> 00:25:20,441
Hard to starboard now.

385
00:25:29,687 --> 00:25:32,563
[dramatic music]

386
00:25:42,040 --> 00:25:43,134
[exhales]

387
00:26:24,712 --> 00:26:26,273
- [knock on door]
- Yeah?

388
00:26:26,375 --> 00:26:28,549
[Mateo] Captain has us
on night shift.

389
00:26:28,651 --> 00:26:30,346
All right, I'll be there
in a sec.

390
00:26:34,952 --> 00:26:37,221
[dramatic music continues]

391
00:27:13,389 --> 00:27:15,292
