396
00:27:40,785 --> 00:27:43,320
[metal groaning]

397
00:27:49,101 --> 00:27:52,527
[faint thumping]

398
00:27:57,099 --> 00:28:00,040
[thumping continues]

399
00:28:04,039 --> 00:28:07,949
[metal groaning]

400
00:28:18,859 --> 00:28:20,698
[woman speaks indistinctly]

401
00:28:26,898 --> 00:28:29,801
[muffled thudding]

402
00:28:29,903 --> 00:28:31,306
[woman speaks indistinctly]

403
00:28:31,408 --> 00:28:33,304
[muffled thudding]

404
00:28:39,316 --> 00:28:42,214
[metal groaning]

405
00:28:44,388 --> 00:28:47,417
[suspenseful music]

406
00:28:53,661 --> 00:28:57,526
[muffled sobbing]

407
00:29:02,331 --> 00:29:03,532
[woman speaks indistinctly]

408
00:29:07,036 --> 00:29:08,739
[muffled cry]

409
00:29:08,841 --> 00:29:09,879
[flashlight clicks]

410
00:29:11,614 --> 00:29:13,377
[Cole exhales sharply]

411
00:29:15,287 --> 00:29:16,248
[flashlight clicks]

412
00:29:18,256 --> 00:29:20,650
[clattering]

413
00:29:20,752 --> 00:29:21,957
[clunks]

414
00:29:29,860 --> 00:29:31,626
[clunks]

415
00:29:34,604 --> 00:29:36,565
- [thud]
- [door squeaks]

416
00:29:39,377 --> 00:29:42,274
[all gasp, whimper]

417
00:29:51,151 --> 00:29:53,357
- [woman mumbles]
- [Cole] It's okay.

418
00:29:53,459 --> 00:29:55,749
It's okay. I'm here to help.

419
00:29:57,594 --> 00:29:58,889
How did you get here?

420
00:29:58,991 --> 00:30:00,724
Does anyone speak English?

421
00:30:00,826 --> 00:30:02,956
Doctor. Doctor.

422
00:30:03,058 --> 00:30:04,329
Doctor.

423
00:30:06,932 --> 00:30:08,468
You speak English?

424
00:30:08,570 --> 00:30:10,539
[man coughs]

425
00:30:10,641 --> 00:30:12,271
How long have you been in here?

426
00:30:12,969 --> 00:30:14,003
Bangkok.

427
00:30:14,105 --> 00:30:15,345
They say they let us out

428
00:30:15,447 --> 00:30:17,138
as soon as leave port,

429
00:30:17,240 --> 00:30:19,373
but they leave us in dark.

430
00:30:19,475 --> 00:30:21,713
- Hot, dark.
- [Cole] Wait, wait.

431
00:30:21,815 --> 00:30:23,744
Please. Sit down.

432
00:30:24,686 --> 00:30:26,046
We need to be quiet.

433
00:30:26,148 --> 00:30:29,582
[speaks Thai]

434
00:30:29,684 --> 00:30:31,325
[Cole in English]
I'm gonna help you.

435
00:30:31,794 --> 00:30:33,127
I'm gonna bring you water...

436
00:30:34,090 --> 00:30:35,497
and food.

437
00:30:35,599 --> 00:30:37,433
Some medical supplies.

438
00:30:37,535 --> 00:30:38,533
[Seng breathes shakily]

439
00:30:38,635 --> 00:30:41,899
[translating in Thai]

440
00:30:42,001 --> 00:30:43,269
[Angie in English] Hello?

441
00:30:45,701 --> 00:30:47,268
[Cole whispering]
You need to trust me.

442
00:30:47,370 --> 00:30:50,542
I'm coming back. For everybody.

443
00:30:50,644 --> 00:30:51,673
Okay?

444
00:30:53,484 --> 00:30:54,943
[lever handle thuds]

445
00:30:55,045 --> 00:30:56,043
[Angie] Hello?

446
00:30:56,145 --> 00:30:59,351
[metal groaning]

447
00:31:06,957 --> 00:31:08,393
Hello?

448
00:31:09,831 --> 00:31:11,297
Is anybody down here?

449
00:31:29,544 --> 00:31:31,952
- [thud]
- [door squeaking]

450
00:31:32,054 --> 00:31:34,215
- [Angie] Oh, my God.
- [all gasp]

451
00:31:34,317 --> 00:31:36,253
Oh, my God. [sniffles]

452
00:31:36,355 --> 00:31:39,252
Okay. It's-it's-- it's okay.
C-come.

453
00:31:39,354 --> 00:31:40,656
Come. One by one.

454
00:31:42,166 --> 00:31:45,059
All right, just-just--
just stay in this area, okay?

455
00:31:45,161 --> 00:31:46,266
We'll help you.

456
00:31:47,066 --> 00:31:48,771
Okay. [breathes sharply]

457
00:31:48,873 --> 00:31:51,073
- Mateo?
- [radio static crackles]

458
00:31:51,870 --> 00:31:52,943
Fuck.

459
00:31:53,943 --> 00:31:56,647
Oh, God.
Your daughter's injured.

460
00:31:56,749 --> 00:31:58,608
Okay, is-is--
is anybody else injured?

461
00:31:59,649 --> 00:32:02,010
[Seng speaks Thai]

462
00:32:02,112 --> 00:32:03,445
[woman coughs]

463
00:32:03,547 --> 00:32:04,851
[in English]
Uh, you with the man?

464
00:32:04,953 --> 00:32:07,788
Uh, he get us food and water

465
00:32:07,890 --> 00:32:09,284
a-and medicine for my daughter.

466
00:32:09,386 --> 00:32:12,259
[Angie] What? W-what man? No.

467
00:32:12,361 --> 00:32:15,362
Look, just... stay calm.
We're gonna help you, all right?

468
00:32:15,464 --> 00:32:17,726
We're gonna get you food and
water. Just-- just stay calm.

469
00:32:18,567 --> 00:32:20,194
Josef!

470
00:32:20,296 --> 00:32:21,695
What's happening?

471
00:32:21,798 --> 00:32:23,334
These people need water
and a medic, all right?

472
00:32:23,436 --> 00:32:24,834
I'm gonna wake the captain.
Go help them.

473
00:32:25,571 --> 00:32:28,168
- Come on, go!
- Yes, I'll-- I'll handle it.

474
00:32:28,270 --> 00:32:31,212
[men whispering]

475
00:32:34,453 --> 00:32:36,580
[knocking on door]

476
00:32:37,713 --> 00:32:39,218
- [water splashes]
- [razor clangs]

477
00:32:39,321 --> 00:32:42,385
[Angie continues knocking]
Captain. Captain!

478
00:32:42,487 --> 00:32:44,021
- [water splashes]
- [razor clangs]

479
00:32:44,123 --> 00:32:45,492
[Angie knocks] Captain?

480
00:32:45,594 --> 00:32:46,656
Hold on.

481
00:32:49,896 --> 00:32:50,959
[towel thumps]

482
00:32:51,428 --> 00:32:52,659
- What is it?
- Captain,

483
00:32:52,761 --> 00:32:54,033
we found
a few dozen people locked

484
00:32:54,135 --> 00:32:55,165
in a container
in the lower hold.

485
00:32:55,267 --> 00:32:57,532
What? Come on in. Come on in.

486
00:32:57,634 --> 00:32:59,702
- They're not in good shape.
- What?

487
00:32:59,804 --> 00:33:02,207
- What-- what's going on?
- They're dehydrated. They're--

488
00:33:02,309 --> 00:33:04,138
[sighs]
Fuck, there's a little girl.

489
00:33:04,240 --> 00:33:05,674
Jesus Christ.

490
00:33:05,776 --> 00:33:07,080
Simon and Josef,
they're down there with them.

491
00:33:07,182 --> 00:33:08,510
- That's good. That's very good.
- Yeah.

492
00:33:08,612 --> 00:33:10,686
Now, calm down
and relax a little bit.

493
00:33:10,788 --> 00:33:12,154
- I'm calm.
- Have a seat.

494
00:33:15,021 --> 00:33:16,518
Captain to bridge.

495
00:33:16,620 --> 00:33:18,188
[Mateo over radio]
<i>Go ahead, sir.</i>

496
00:33:18,290 --> 00:33:19,653
Ellis found some people locked

497
00:33:19,755 --> 00:33:22,059
in one of the lower
container holds.

498
00:33:22,161 --> 00:33:23,496
She's here with me now.

499
00:33:23,932 --> 00:33:25,731
Let's follow protocol.

500
00:33:25,833 --> 00:33:26,960
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

501
00:33:28,836 --> 00:33:29,800
[radio thuds]

502
00:33:30,536 --> 00:33:32,700
- We should call the navy, sir.
- Yes, I will.

503
00:33:32,802 --> 00:33:34,934
But let's find out
what's going on first.

504
00:33:35,036 --> 00:33:36,943
I think it's pretty clear
what's going on, sir.

505
00:33:37,045 --> 00:33:39,046
I hear you, and we got this.

506
00:33:39,148 --> 00:33:40,443
I'm gonna get a hold
of the doctor

507
00:33:40,545 --> 00:33:41,874
and you can guide him down,
okay?

508
00:33:41,977 --> 00:33:43,112
-<i> Jones for Captain.</i>
- Sit down and relax.

509
00:33:43,214 --> 00:33:44,412
You did a good job.

510
00:33:44,514 --> 00:33:46,155
Very good. Please sit down.

511
00:33:47,359 --> 00:33:48,322
Sure.

512
00:33:49,384 --> 00:33:50,891
Marko. Come in.

513
00:33:50,993 --> 00:33:52,557
<i>Do you need assistance, sir?</i>

514
00:33:53,225 --> 00:33:55,089
No. Ellis is with me.

515
00:33:55,858 --> 00:33:58,398
And Mateo is-- is handling
protocol below.

516
00:33:59,729 --> 00:34:02,032
Maintain your position, please.
Thank you.

517
00:34:02,134 --> 00:34:03,469
<i>Roger that, sir.</i>

518
00:34:07,542 --> 00:34:10,140
[Josef] Everyone, get back
in the container. Let's go.

519
00:34:10,242 --> 00:34:11,408
[migrants speaking Thai]

520
00:34:11,510 --> 00:34:13,407
[Josef in English]
All of you, move.

521
00:34:13,509 --> 00:34:15,383
Get the fuck back inside.

522
00:34:15,485 --> 00:34:16,416
Now!

523
00:34:17,347 --> 00:34:19,054
[migrants yelping]

524
00:34:19,156 --> 00:34:21,289
- I said, get back in.
- [Simon] Get back!

525
00:34:21,391 --> 00:34:22,955
- [Josef] I said, get back in!
- [migrants screaming]

526
00:34:23,057 --> 00:34:24,886
Get back in the container!

527
00:34:25,589 --> 00:34:27,658
- Get back!
- [woman yelping]

528
00:34:29,933 --> 00:34:30,962
[migrants continue screaming]

529
00:34:31,064 --> 00:34:32,597
I said, get back in!

530
00:34:33,835 --> 00:34:35,171
[Seng gasps]

531
00:34:36,607 --> 00:34:38,933
[Josef grunting]

532
00:34:40,910 --> 00:34:42,774
- You!
- [speaks Thai]

533
00:34:42,877 --> 00:34:44,339
[grunting]

534
00:34:44,441 --> 00:34:47,216
Aah! [yelling in pain]

535
00:34:48,377 --> 00:34:50,749
[grunting]

536
00:34:50,852 --> 00:34:51,847
[gunshots]

537
00:34:56,395 --> 00:34:57,358
[grunts]

538
00:35:03,030 --> 00:35:04,829
[grunts, whimpers]

539
00:35:05,532 --> 00:35:06,801
[in English] Hey,
something's not right.

540
00:35:06,903 --> 00:35:08,334
We need to call the navy.

541
00:35:08,436 --> 00:35:09,701
- The captain just isn't--
- [gun cocks]

542
00:35:10,404 --> 00:35:11,867
[Mateo] We're not calling
anybody.

543
00:35:12,907 --> 00:35:13,869
[radio beeps]

544
00:35:14,943 --> 00:35:16,036
Mateo to Captain.

545
00:35:17,208 --> 00:35:18,340
Go for Captain.

546
00:35:18,442 --> 00:35:19,479
Got her on the bridge.

547
00:35:20,475 --> 00:35:21,745
I'm on my way.

548
00:35:23,280 --> 00:35:24,253
[knife rasps]

549
00:35:25,451 --> 00:35:28,551
- [yells]
- [both grunting]

550
00:35:28,653 --> 00:35:32,054
- [Josef groans in pain]
- [both grunting]

551
00:35:32,156 --> 00:35:33,460
[grunts]

552
00:35:35,457 --> 00:35:38,630
[both grunting]

553
00:35:39,164 --> 00:35:40,561
Step back.

554
00:35:40,664 --> 00:35:42,467
- Sit the fuck down.
- Okay.

555
00:35:42,569 --> 00:35:43,797
- [radio static crackles]
- [Angie grunts]

556
00:35:43,899 --> 00:35:46,308
- [gun clatters]
- [both grunting]

557
00:35:51,583 --> 00:35:55,145
[both grunting]

558
00:35:55,247 --> 00:35:56,984
[Josef straining]

559
00:35:57,087 --> 00:35:59,479
- Aah! [grunts]
- [Cole grunts]

560
00:35:59,581 --> 00:36:01,455
[screaming in pain]

561
00:36:03,586 --> 00:36:06,321
[yells, grunts in pain]

562
00:36:06,423 --> 00:36:07,663
[migrants screaming]

563
00:36:07,765 --> 00:36:09,564
[Dara speaks Thai]

564
00:36:09,667 --> 00:36:10,695
[gunshots]

565
00:36:12,868 --> 00:36:13,830
[Simon] Aah!

566
00:36:22,808 --> 00:36:24,045
[in English] We need to get you
off of this ship

567
00:36:24,147 --> 00:36:25,613
before the rest of them
get here.

568
00:36:26,183 --> 00:36:28,180
We need to go up
to the lifeboats.

569
00:36:28,282 --> 00:36:30,410
Stay close. Stay behind me.

570
00:36:30,512 --> 00:36:31,650
Let's move.

571
00:36:32,715 --> 00:36:35,324
[migrants conversing in Thai]

572
00:36:38,630 --> 00:36:40,659
[tense music]

573
00:36:41,863 --> 00:36:42,861
Fuck.

574
00:36:42,963 --> 00:36:43,962
[beeps]

575
00:36:44,064 --> 00:36:46,368
[signal beeping]

576
00:37:06,658 --> 00:37:07,653
[Angie] Aah!

577
00:37:08,858 --> 00:37:09,820
[Angie grunts]

578
00:37:10,353 --> 00:37:11,426
Come on.

579
00:37:14,827 --> 00:37:16,294
- Go fucking get her. Now.
- [crewman] Yes, sir.

580
00:37:16,396 --> 00:37:17,627
- Move!
- [Mateo groaning]

581
00:37:17,729 --> 00:37:20,168
What the fuck are you doing?
Get up!

582
00:37:20,270 --> 00:37:22,830
What the fuck's wrong
with you, huh?

583
00:37:22,932 --> 00:37:24,204
[Mateo]
It's still transmitting, sir.

584
00:37:24,306 --> 00:37:25,734
[Marko] Then cancel it,
you idiot.

585
00:37:25,836 --> 00:37:27,742
- [buttons click]
- Signal canceled, sir.

586
00:37:27,844 --> 00:37:29,077
We're okay.

587
00:37:29,179 --> 00:37:31,006
We're pretty fucking far
from okay.

588
00:37:31,108 --> 00:37:33,013
Now, get your sorry ass down
and disable the lifeboats

589
00:37:33,115 --> 00:37:34,110
so she can't get away.

590
00:37:34,213 --> 00:37:35,285
Yes, sir.

591
00:37:36,779 --> 00:37:37,953
And where the fuck is Jonathan?

592
00:37:38,055 --> 00:37:40,086
I'm on it, sir. Jorge, come in.

593
00:37:40,188 --> 00:37:42,622
[tense music continues]

594
00:37:53,771 --> 00:37:55,096
Ah! Fuck.

595
00:38:00,909 --> 00:38:02,204
Come on.

596
00:38:02,307 --> 00:38:03,412
Hey, you.

597
00:38:05,646 --> 00:38:07,109
You know how to use
one of these things?

598
00:38:07,211 --> 00:38:08,142
Yes.

599
00:38:09,154 --> 00:38:10,648
- Okay, listen.
- [Seng mumbles in Thai]

600
00:38:10,750 --> 00:38:12,383
I'm gonna look
for the woman who found you.

601
00:38:12,485 --> 00:38:14,154
I think she might be in trouble.

602
00:38:14,257 --> 00:38:16,458
- Don't wait for me.
- Okay.

603
00:38:28,599 --> 00:38:30,235
Captain on the bridge.

604
00:38:30,337 --> 00:38:31,573
[Spencer] As you were.

605
00:38:32,176 --> 00:38:34,210
- Good morning.
- Morning, sir.

606
00:38:34,312 --> 00:38:36,404
Distress call came in
from a cargo ship.

607
00:38:36,506 --> 00:38:38,343
KMG Artemis.

608
00:38:38,445 --> 00:38:40,048
Nine degrees, 49 minutes north,

609
00:38:40,150 --> 00:38:42,478
92 degrees, 56 minutes east.

610
00:38:42,580 --> 00:38:44,483
05:33 hours local time.

611
00:38:44,585 --> 00:38:47,189
That's the edge
of the Andaman Sea.

612
00:38:47,291 --> 00:38:49,491
- What was the code?
- Attack, sir.

613
00:38:50,257 --> 00:38:52,590
An attack? By who?

614
00:38:52,692 --> 00:38:54,424
Last I checked,
we were 600 miles east

615
00:38:54,526 --> 00:38:55,524
of any pirate activity.

616
00:38:55,626 --> 00:38:56,756
They canceled the call

617
00:38:56,858 --> 00:38:58,563
before we could respond.

618
00:38:58,665 --> 00:39:00,337
Must have been
some kind of mistake.

619
00:39:01,138 --> 00:39:02,831
[clicks tongue, inhales sharply]

620
00:39:02,933 --> 00:39:04,603
Let's give 'em a call back,
Yates.

621
00:39:04,705 --> 00:39:06,937
- Make sure everything's kosher.
- Yes, sir.

622
00:39:09,475 --> 00:39:10,906
Artemis, Artemis, Artemis.

623
00:39:11,008 --> 00:39:14,415
This is the USS Hazard Perry
on Channel 16.

624
00:39:14,517 --> 00:39:16,242
[over radio]
<i>Artemis, Artemis, Artemis.</i>

625
00:39:16,344 --> 00:39:19,617
<i>This is the USS Hazard Perry</i>
<i>on Channel 16.</i>

626
00:39:19,719 --> 00:39:21,457
-<i> Artemis, Artemis, Artemis.</i>
- Tsk.

627
00:39:22,189 --> 00:39:23,223
[radio beeps]

628
00:39:23,325 --> 00:39:25,186
Hazard Perry, this is Artemis.

629
00:39:26,792 --> 00:39:28,561
Good morning.
This is Captain Spencer

630
00:39:28,663 --> 00:39:31,064
of the USS Hazard Perry.
Who am I talking to?

631
00:39:31,633 --> 00:39:34,368
This is Marko Madsen,
captain of the Artemis.

632
00:39:34,470 --> 00:39:36,437
You must have gotten
our DSC call.

633
00:39:36,539 --> 00:39:37,566
[Spencer over radio]
<i>Yeah, we sure did.</i>

634
00:39:37,668 --> 00:39:38,805
<i>So, what happened there?</i>

635
00:39:39,340 --> 00:39:40,404
I'm sorry, one of my guys

636
00:39:40,506 --> 00:39:42,211
spotted light in our wake.

637
00:39:42,313 --> 00:39:43,713
He had a run-in
with some Somalis

638
00:39:43,815 --> 00:39:45,112
a few years ago.

639
00:39:45,214 --> 00:39:46,179
You know how that goes.

640
00:39:46,281 --> 00:39:47,277
Got a little trigger-happy

641
00:39:47,379 --> 00:39:48,978
with the DSC.

642
00:39:49,080 --> 00:39:50,849
But it turns out,
it was just a fishing vessel.

643
00:39:53,658 --> 00:39:55,821
You're pretty far out for
a fishing vessel, aren't you?

644
00:39:57,362 --> 00:39:59,258
Must-- must have been
a deep-sea trawler.

645
00:39:59,360 --> 00:40:00,760
Not the first one we see.

646
00:40:02,727 --> 00:40:04,599
<i>Sorry to waste the navy's time.</i>

647
00:40:07,602 --> 00:40:10,033
Not at all.
Glad everyone's okay.

648
00:40:12,767 --> 00:40:13,740
[radio thuds]

649
00:40:16,039 --> 00:40:18,243
[Jamai] You have no idea
where he could be?

650
00:40:18,345 --> 00:40:19,476
No clue, I'm afraid.

651
00:40:19,578 --> 00:40:20,641
We have a call to you

652
00:40:20,743 --> 00:40:22,018
from a burner phone,

653
00:40:22,120 --> 00:40:23,984
shortly after the accident,

654
00:40:24,086 --> 00:40:25,180
near the port.

655
00:40:26,957 --> 00:40:28,018
Who called you?

656
00:40:29,422 --> 00:40:31,319
I... don't recall.

657
00:40:32,122 --> 00:40:33,853
To be honest, I--
I don't even remember

658
00:40:33,955 --> 00:40:35,096
receiving the phone call.

659
00:40:35,198 --> 00:40:37,192
There was a lot going on.

660
00:40:40,135 --> 00:40:41,462
Okay, well,

661
00:40:42,232 --> 00:40:44,906
please let us know
if you remember anything, or...

662
00:40:45,542 --> 00:40:47,642
if any further information
comes to light.

663
00:40:48,540 --> 00:40:49,942
As you can imagine,

664
00:40:50,745 --> 00:40:53,945
your father's murder
is our highest priority.

665
00:40:55,546 --> 00:40:56,915
Of course.

666
00:40:58,615 --> 00:41:00,886
[tense music]

667
00:41:15,601 --> 00:41:17,500
[indistinct murmuring]

668
00:41:17,602 --> 00:41:20,070
[running footsteps]

669
00:41:25,114 --> 00:41:26,673
[Angie grunts]

670
00:41:26,775 --> 00:41:28,744
[Cole shushing]

671
00:41:28,846 --> 00:41:30,619
[Cole] You're okay. Trust me.

672
00:41:31,453 --> 00:41:34,689
[Angie gasps, breathing heavily]

673
00:41:35,322 --> 00:41:36,350
[Cole] Open it.

674
00:41:36,961 --> 00:41:37,923
[Angie grunts]

675
00:41:40,189 --> 00:41:42,197
- [door closes]
- [lever handle clunks]

676
00:41:42,299 --> 00:41:43,559
[Angie] Who the fuck are you?

677
00:41:43,661 --> 00:41:45,058
I'm not one of them.

678
00:41:45,160 --> 00:41:46,329
Right now,
that's all that matters.

679
00:41:46,432 --> 00:41:47,499
[panting]

680
00:41:47,601 --> 00:41:49,005
There are people in the hold,

681
00:41:49,107 --> 00:41:50,172
and they're in danger.

682
00:41:50,274 --> 00:41:52,034
They're not gonna kill them,

683
00:41:52,136 --> 00:41:53,507
not when they're making money
off of them.

684
00:41:53,609 --> 00:41:54,602
You don't know
what they're gonna do.

685
00:41:54,704 --> 00:41:56,172
They shot me.

686
00:42:01,779 --> 00:42:02,849
[indistinct radio chatter]

687
00:42:05,551 --> 00:42:09,389
[woman speaks Thai]

688
00:42:09,491 --> 00:42:11,726
[migrants conversing in Thai]

689
00:42:15,563 --> 00:42:16,790
- [gunshot]
- [Dara] Aah!

690
00:42:16,892 --> 00:42:18,197
[migrants screaming]

691
00:42:18,299 --> 00:42:19,534
Check for more.

692
00:42:19,636 --> 00:42:21,400
Everybody, let's go!
Out of the lifeboat!

693
00:42:21,502 --> 00:42:23,266
[screaming continues]

694
00:42:23,835 --> 00:42:25,366
[Angie] We need to help them.

695
00:42:26,340 --> 00:42:27,773
[Cole] We will.

696
00:42:27,875 --> 00:42:30,077
But first, we need to take care
of that wound.

697
00:42:30,179 --> 00:42:32,373
Come. This way.

698
00:42:37,648 --> 00:42:39,182
Down there.

699
00:42:41,256 --> 00:42:44,319
[action music]

700
00:42:54,237 --> 00:42:55,605
[exhales sharply]

701
00:43:00,408 --> 00:43:01,842
[Diego hisses] Shit.

702
00:43:40,711 --> 00:43:43,246
[tense music]

703
00:43:52,392 --> 00:43:53,927
[groans]

704
00:43:56,000 --> 00:43:57,095
Come on.

705
00:44:00,571 --> 00:44:02,430
I found Jonathan's stuff
in a lifeboat.

706
00:44:05,804 --> 00:44:07,472
Josef and Simon are dead.

707
00:44:07,574 --> 00:44:09,239
- What?
- Yeah.

708
00:44:11,681 --> 00:44:13,043
They were serious players,
Captain.

709
00:44:13,145 --> 00:44:14,978
Whoever did this
had to be a professional.

710
00:44:15,080 --> 00:44:17,212
It can't be Ellis.
She's fleet navy.

711
00:44:17,315 --> 00:44:18,850
No combat experience.
And even if she did--

712
00:44:18,952 --> 00:44:21,185
[Marko] Still,
she took you out, right?

713
00:44:23,589 --> 00:44:24,821
Sweep the ship.

714
00:44:24,923 --> 00:44:26,919
Find out who the fuck's came on.

715
00:44:27,021 --> 00:44:28,126
Yes, Captain.

716
00:44:31,762 --> 00:44:33,703
[keypad beeping]

717
00:44:36,704 --> 00:44:38,367
We got a problem on the ship.

718
00:44:39,506 --> 00:44:42,107
[loud whirring]

719
00:44:51,352 --> 00:44:52,480
[grunts]

720
00:44:59,526 --> 00:45:00,653
[Angie] Here.

721
00:45:04,498 --> 00:45:06,466
[headsets beep]

722
00:45:06,568 --> 00:45:09,970
[Angie breathing heavily]

723
00:45:14,203 --> 00:45:15,872
[over headset] I've seen worse.

724
00:45:15,974 --> 00:45:17,571
[Angie] I saw you on the news.

725
00:45:18,547 --> 00:45:19,908
I know you're on the run.

726
00:45:20,344 --> 00:45:22,776
Are you at least gonna tell me
your name?

727
00:45:22,879 --> 00:45:24,220
Cole Reed.

728
00:45:24,322 --> 00:45:26,385
[sighs] Okay, Cole Reed.

729
00:45:26,487 --> 00:45:27,724
I'm Angie Ellis.

730
00:45:29,183 --> 00:45:30,859
Okay, Angie Ellis.

731
00:45:31,658 --> 00:45:33,762
This is gonna hurt.

732
00:45:33,864 --> 00:45:35,330
Maybe you wanna talk,
take your mind off of it.

733
00:45:35,432 --> 00:45:36,565
No. [exhales sharply]

734
00:45:36,667 --> 00:45:37,563
Tell me something
about yourself.

735
00:45:37,665 --> 00:45:39,134
[Angie breathes sharply]

736
00:45:39,236 --> 00:45:41,263
Aah! Fuck me!

737
00:45:41,365 --> 00:45:43,602
- You have a family?
- [breathes sharply]

738
00:45:43,704 --> 00:45:45,466
I have a deadbeat ex,

739
00:45:45,568 --> 00:45:47,502
and the most wonderful
little girl in the world.

740
00:45:49,004 --> 00:45:50,409
What's her name?

741
00:45:50,511 --> 00:45:51,572
[Angie] Violet.

742
00:45:52,942 --> 00:45:54,281
Great name.

743
00:45:54,383 --> 00:45:55,849
How old is she?

744
00:45:55,951 --> 00:45:58,186
[Angie breathes sharply]
She just turned six.

745
00:45:58,288 --> 00:46:00,345
[yells in pain]

746
00:46:00,448 --> 00:46:01,486
- Fuck!
- Try to hold still.

747
00:46:01,588 --> 00:46:02,891
[Angie] Oh!

748
00:46:03,524 --> 00:46:06,360
[Angie grunting]

749
00:46:06,462 --> 00:46:07,856
[relieved exhale]

750
00:46:07,958 --> 00:46:09,227
Fuck, that hurts!

751
00:46:10,128 --> 00:46:11,760
- Oh, fuck.
- [bullet clatters]

752
00:46:11,862 --> 00:46:12,994
[relieved sigh]

753
00:46:13,096 --> 00:46:15,264
Oh, my God. [exhales]

754
00:46:15,366 --> 00:46:17,433
[Cole] Share custody
with Mr. Deadbeat Ex?

755
00:46:18,968 --> 00:46:20,407
[Angie] No.

756
00:46:20,509 --> 00:46:21,867
[inhales sharply]

757
00:46:21,969 --> 00:46:23,203
Oh!

758
00:46:23,305 --> 00:46:25,176
I used to share partial custody,

759
00:46:25,278 --> 00:46:27,476
but then I lost it
when I got fired from the navy.

760
00:46:28,583 --> 00:46:30,644
[breathes deeply]

761
00:46:30,746 --> 00:46:32,687
I promised her I'd be back
more than two days a month,

762
00:46:32,789 --> 00:46:34,847
and I--
I can't even fucking do that.

763
00:46:35,416 --> 00:46:37,420
[sighs] There's still time.

764
00:46:40,255 --> 00:46:42,792
- Okay.
- [grunts]

765
00:46:42,894 --> 00:46:44,394
[breathes deeply]

766
00:46:52,567 --> 00:46:54,173
I need backup
at the engine room.

767
00:46:56,173 --> 00:46:58,241
- Oh. Yeah.
- [Cole] Okay?

768
00:46:58,344 --> 00:46:59,546
- We need to keep moving.
- Okay, I got it.

769
00:46:59,648 --> 00:47:02,547
Yeah. I got it. I'm good.

770
00:47:02,649 --> 00:47:05,316
[loud whirring]

771
00:47:18,926 --> 00:47:20,861
[over headset] She was here.
She couldn't have got far.

772
00:47:20,963 --> 00:47:22,201
Move.

773
00:47:32,781 --> 00:47:34,749
Any fishing boat this far out

774
00:47:34,851 --> 00:47:36,512
would be registered
on AIS, right?

775
00:47:37,046 --> 00:47:38,080
Yes, sir.

776
00:47:38,182 --> 00:47:39,378
Let's check and see what traffic

777
00:47:39,480 --> 00:47:40,854
was near the Artemis's position

778
00:47:40,956 --> 00:47:42,855
- around the time of the call.
- Sir.

779
00:47:42,957 --> 00:47:44,460
And, uh, see
what you can drum up

780
00:47:44,562 --> 00:47:47,325
on this Captain Marko Madsen.

781
00:47:58,001 --> 00:47:59,265
Hey, hey.

782
00:47:59,367 --> 00:48:00,976
What happened in Bangkok?

783
00:48:01,078 --> 00:48:02,634
On the news, they said
you're Campallo's bodyguard.

784
00:48:02,736 --> 00:48:05,271
Did you kill him?
Did you kill those cops?

785
00:48:05,373 --> 00:48:06,910
Why are you on the ship?

786
00:48:07,012 --> 00:48:08,346
That is not what happened.

787
00:48:10,151 --> 00:48:11,487
Right now, all that matters
is we get you

788
00:48:11,589 --> 00:48:12,922
and those people to safety.

789
00:48:14,724 --> 00:48:16,283
I sent out a distress signal.

790
00:48:16,385 --> 00:48:17,588
I don't know if anyone got it.

791
00:48:18,325 --> 00:48:20,160
There's no cell service
on the ship, but I know

792
00:48:20,262 --> 00:48:22,421
that there are sat phones
and radios on the bridge.

793
00:48:22,523 --> 00:48:23,799
Then that's where we need to go.

794
00:48:23,901 --> 00:48:24,960
If we go to the bridge,
every man on the ship

795
00:48:25,062 --> 00:48:26,166
will come running.

796
00:48:26,666 --> 00:48:27,897
[sighs]

797
00:48:27,999 --> 00:48:29,664
We need a diversion.

798
00:48:32,068 --> 00:48:33,938
[tense music]

799
00:48:34,040 --> 00:48:35,373
[Angie] In the last cargo hold.

800
00:48:36,479 --> 00:48:37,540
This way.

801
00:48:42,716 --> 00:48:43,777
It's here.

802
00:48:46,748 --> 00:48:48,823
- [handle clanks, squeaks]
- [Angie grunts]

803
00:48:48,925 --> 00:48:50,289
- [Angie] Ah.
- Here, let me help.

804
00:48:50,955 --> 00:48:53,193
[handle clunks]

805
00:48:54,124 --> 00:48:57,857
[doors squeaking]

806
00:48:59,802 --> 00:49:01,463
[Cole] What about the refugees?

807
00:49:01,565 --> 00:49:03,196
In an emergency,
every section of this boat

808
00:49:03,298 --> 00:49:04,339
can be sealed off.

809
00:49:04,441 --> 00:49:05,601
They'll be safe.

810
00:49:13,483 --> 00:49:15,446
[ripping]

811
00:49:21,550 --> 00:49:23,556
- [lighter closes]
- Let's go.

812
00:49:23,658 --> 00:49:26,226
[tense music]

813
00:49:37,333 --> 00:49:38,766
[indistinct radio chatter]

814
00:49:42,138 --> 00:49:44,673
[fire crackling]

815
00:49:46,274 --> 00:49:51,586
[alarm blaring]

816
00:49:51,688 --> 00:49:53,522
Fire on five. Seal it off.

817
00:49:53,992 --> 00:49:55,750
- Initiate fire protocol.
- [buttons click]

818
00:49:56,660 --> 00:49:57,855
Listen up, everybody.

819
00:49:57,957 --> 00:50:00,154
This is a diversion.

820
00:50:00,256 --> 00:50:01,588
We have a stowaway.

821
00:50:01,690 --> 00:50:04,496
I want two guards
at each tower door.

822
00:50:05,433 --> 00:50:08,769
Diego, I want you to oversee
and patrol the towers.

823
00:50:08,871 --> 00:50:10,771
- Yes, sir.
- [Marko] Mateo,

824
00:50:10,873 --> 00:50:12,167
you go down with the fire team.

825
00:50:12,269 --> 00:50:13,671
I'll surveil the deck.

826
00:50:13,774 --> 00:50:14,840
Yes, sir.

827
00:50:14,942 --> 00:50:17,178
[tense music continues]

828
00:50:19,307 --> 00:50:20,346
[gun cocks]

829
00:50:38,803 --> 00:50:39,967
[crewman]
A fire on the high seas.

830
00:50:40,069 --> 00:50:41,295
That's definitely
the worst thing

831
00:50:41,397 --> 00:50:42,632
you can have out here.

832
00:50:44,838 --> 00:50:46,541
[fire roaring]

833
00:50:46,643 --> 00:50:47,967
Increase pressure!

834
00:50:56,314 --> 00:50:57,581
- [loud clang]
- [exhales]

835
00:50:59,690 --> 00:51:01,883
[fire continues roaring]

836
00:51:01,985 --> 00:51:03,756
- It's the batteries, sir.
- [Marko over radio]<i> Contain it.</i>

837
00:51:03,858 --> 00:51:04,984
I'm going up top.

838
00:51:06,587 --> 00:51:09,395
[tense music continues]

839
00:51:14,165 --> 00:51:16,600
[breathing heavily]

840
00:51:47,263 --> 00:51:48,566
[loud clang]

841
00:52:12,829 --> 00:52:14,356
[crewman 1 gasps, grunts]

842
00:52:14,459 --> 00:52:16,523
[crewman 1] Aah!
[grunts in pain]

843
00:52:16,625 --> 00:52:18,330
- [grunts]
- [bones snap]

844
00:52:18,432 --> 00:52:20,169
- [body thuds]
- [radio static crackles]

845
00:52:23,332 --> 00:52:24,706
[beeping]

846
00:52:24,808 --> 00:52:26,073
Mayday, Mayday, Mayday.

847
00:52:26,175 --> 00:52:28,441
This is the KMG Artemis.
Please respond.

848
00:52:29,680 --> 00:52:31,470
All posts report.

849
00:52:31,572 --> 00:52:33,007
All posts report.

850
00:52:33,476 --> 00:52:35,008
Portside secure, sir.

851
00:52:35,110 --> 00:52:36,413
[crewman 2 over radio]<i> Starboard</i>
<i>entrance is secure, sir.</i>

852
00:52:36,515 --> 00:52:38,985
This is the KMG Artemis.
Please respond.

853
00:52:39,088 --> 00:52:40,250
[Mateo]<i> Fire contained, Captain.</i>

854
00:52:40,352 --> 00:52:42,323
Seal the hold. Return to deck.

855
00:52:45,591 --> 00:52:48,420
[Angie] This is the KMG Artemis
on Channel 9.

856
00:52:48,522 --> 00:52:50,122
Please respond.

857
00:52:52,927 --> 00:52:54,998
This is the KMG Artemis
on Channel 16.

858
00:52:55,100 --> 00:52:56,635
Please respond.

859
00:52:57,170 --> 00:52:59,538
Captain to bridge. Report.

860
00:53:01,703 --> 00:53:03,707
We're about to be short on time.

861
00:53:07,146 --> 00:53:08,417
Captain to bridge.

862
00:53:08,519 --> 00:53:09,575
<i>Report.</i>

863
00:53:09,677 --> 00:53:11,451
- Shit.
- [beeps]

864
00:53:14,990 --> 00:53:16,955
[tense music intensifies]

865
00:53:17,057 --> 00:53:18,293
[exhales sharply]

866
00:53:21,022 --> 00:53:23,298
They're on the bridge.
Diego, get up there.

867
00:53:26,032 --> 00:53:27,335
[footsteps]

868
00:53:29,234 --> 00:53:30,470
[Cole] Keep quiet.

869
00:53:31,808 --> 00:53:34,870
[suspenseful music]

870
00:53:46,081 --> 00:53:49,219
This is Captain Spencer
of the USS Hazard Perry.

871
00:53:49,321 --> 00:53:50,985
[Diego exclaims, yells]

872
00:53:52,729 --> 00:53:55,187
[Diego grunting]

873
00:53:57,057 --> 00:53:59,235
[radio feedback squeals,
static crackles]

874
00:53:59,337 --> 00:54:00,960
[Angie] Commander Spencer,
this is the KMG Artemis.

875
00:54:01,062 --> 00:54:02,596
We need immediate
emergency assistance.

876
00:54:02,698 --> 00:54:03,830
[Marko shouting indistinctly]

877
00:54:03,932 --> 00:54:05,436
Who am I talking to
and who is "we"?

878
00:54:05,538 --> 00:54:06,899
[over radio]
<i>My name is Angie Ellis.</i>

879
00:54:07,001 --> 00:54:08,671
I'm the third mate
on the Artemis.

880
00:54:08,773 --> 00:54:11,172
I'm with a man named Cole Reed.
We need help.

881
00:54:12,108 --> 00:54:14,116
The captain is running
a human trafficking operation.

882
00:54:14,218 --> 00:54:16,844
Our position
is latitude 45 degrees north,

883
00:54:16,946 --> 00:54:18,744
- longitude 155 east.
- We need to move.

884
00:54:18,846 --> 00:54:21,257
- Now.
- Send help! Fast!

885
00:54:25,259 --> 00:54:26,828
[Yates] Was that gunfire, sir?

886
00:54:26,930 --> 00:54:28,460
Get me that dossier. Now.

887
00:54:28,562 --> 00:54:30,489
- Set course for the Artemis.
- Yes, sir.

888
00:54:30,591 --> 00:54:33,302
[tense music]

889
00:54:36,096 --> 00:54:37,768
[Angie] Come on.
We're going to my cabin.

890
00:54:41,971 --> 00:54:43,471
We should be able
to get down from here.

891
00:54:43,573 --> 00:54:45,644
[indistinct radio chatter]

892
00:54:49,085 --> 00:54:50,418
[Cole] They're right outside.

893
00:54:54,924 --> 00:54:58,520
[breathing shakily]

894
00:54:58,622 --> 00:55:00,296
[Angie] If I-- If I don't...

895
00:55:01,060 --> 00:55:02,291
Oh, God.

896
00:55:02,393 --> 00:55:03,596
[Cole] Here, sit.

897
00:55:05,797 --> 00:55:07,628
- Look at me.
- [continues breathing shakily]

898
00:55:07,730 --> 00:55:09,129
I'm gonna get you back to her.

899
00:55:10,136 --> 00:55:11,263
I promise.

900
00:55:12,138 --> 00:55:14,469
Mm. Okay.

901
00:55:14,571 --> 00:55:16,807
[tense music continues]

902
00:55:26,616 --> 00:55:27,983
Bigger cut for each of us.

903
00:55:29,927 --> 00:55:31,585
All right, listen up.

904
00:55:31,687 --> 00:55:33,060
There is no stowaway.

905
00:55:33,162 --> 00:55:34,521
That's Campallo's bodyguard.

906
00:55:35,091 --> 00:55:37,022
[over radio]
<i>So, there's a change of plans.</i>

907
00:55:37,124 --> 00:55:40,058
<i>Going in two hours,</i>
<i>ship to ship.</i>

908
00:55:40,160 --> 00:55:41,731
- What's in two hours?
- I don't know.

909
00:55:41,833 --> 00:55:43,330
- [Marko] Understood?
- [all] Yes, sir.

910
00:55:43,432 --> 00:55:44,373
Move.

911
00:55:55,852 --> 00:55:58,618
[phone buzzing]

912
00:56:01,319 --> 00:56:02,918
Go ahead.

913
00:56:03,020 --> 00:56:04,222
[Marko over phone]
<i>What the fuck is Cole Reed</i>

914
00:56:04,324 --> 00:56:06,290
<i>doing on my ship, huh?</i>

915
00:56:06,392 --> 00:56:08,159
<i>How is he even alive?</i>

916
00:56:08,895 --> 00:56:10,993
<i>I thought we took care of him</i>
<i>when we killed Tibu.</i>

917
00:56:11,959 --> 00:56:13,127
<i>What the fuck's going on?</i>

918
00:56:14,863 --> 00:56:17,197
Look, the kill team fucked up.

919
00:56:18,231 --> 00:56:20,770
Don't let him fuck up
the transaction.

920
00:56:20,872 --> 00:56:23,373
<i>He won't.</i>
<i>We moved up the delivery.</i>

921
00:56:23,475 --> 00:56:25,078
<i>I've contacted Bertus.</i>

922
00:56:25,180 --> 00:56:26,978
<i>He's two hours away.</i>

923
00:56:27,080 --> 00:56:28,044
Fine.

924
00:56:28,580 --> 00:56:30,084
Just make sure that Cole Reed

925
00:56:30,186 --> 00:56:31,950
doesn't get off that ship alive.

926
00:56:32,052 --> 00:56:33,284
<i>I will.</i>

927
00:56:33,386 --> 00:56:34,451
You're gonna owe me extra

928
00:56:34,553 --> 00:56:36,056
for dealing with this thug.

929
00:56:36,158 --> 00:56:37,987
Any updates on Kameron?

930
00:56:38,590 --> 00:56:40,319
<i>Are we still in business?</i>

931
00:56:41,064 --> 00:56:42,354
The sale has been halted.

932
00:56:43,495 --> 00:56:44,730
It's business as usual.

933
00:56:46,496 --> 00:56:47,560
What is it?

934
00:56:47,662 --> 00:56:48,767
Who's Kameron?

935
00:56:49,930 --> 00:56:51,237
Kameron's Tibu's son.

936
00:56:51,339 --> 00:56:52,774
And you think he's involved?

937
00:56:52,876 --> 00:56:53,937
I don't know.

938
00:56:54,869 --> 00:56:56,270
But Marko's involved.

939
00:56:57,073 --> 00:56:58,447
- And he's gonna pay.
- [crewman] Move.

940
00:56:59,610 --> 00:57:00,944
Couldn't have got far.

941
00:57:01,742 --> 00:57:03,177
It's time to go.

942
00:57:08,023 --> 00:57:11,053
[tense music]

943
00:57:12,753 --> 00:57:14,124
[Angie grunts]

944
00:57:14,227 --> 00:57:15,794
[gunshots]

945
00:57:19,034 --> 00:57:21,470
[wind whooshing]

946
00:57:27,040 --> 00:57:29,810
[Cole]<i> Until the navy gets here,</i>
<i>those migrants aren't safe.</i>

947
00:57:30,245 --> 00:57:31,676
We need to get below deck.

948
00:57:31,779 --> 00:57:33,178
There are lots of places
to hide 'em down there,

949
00:57:33,280 --> 00:57:34,378
but you heard him,

950
00:57:34,480 --> 00:57:35,616
they're all being guarded.

951
00:57:36,483 --> 00:57:37,783
There's gotta be another way.

952
00:57:39,213 --> 00:57:41,490
We could try
the ventilation shaft.

953
00:57:42,786 --> 00:57:44,883
Sir, the dossier you requested.

954
00:57:45,486 --> 00:57:48,454
Marko's been with KMG
for 13 years, captain for ten.

955
00:57:48,990 --> 00:57:50,626
Danish national, Jaeger Corps.

956
00:57:50,728 --> 00:57:52,032
Tours in Afghanistan, Iraq.

957
00:57:52,134 --> 00:57:53,499
Investigated twice.

958
00:57:53,601 --> 00:57:55,400
Allegations of looting
and smuggling.

959
00:57:55,970 --> 00:57:58,031
They thought he killed one
of his teammates on a mission,

960
00:57:58,133 --> 00:57:59,503
but the rest of the unit
wasn't talking.

961
00:57:59,606 --> 00:58:01,675
- Nothing stuck.
- And his crew?

962
00:58:01,777 --> 00:58:05,044
Half of them are either
ex-military or ex-mercenary.

963
00:58:05,146 --> 00:58:06,573
Spanish MEO,

964
00:58:06,675 --> 00:58:09,209
Irish AOW, GRU.

965
00:58:09,311 --> 00:58:11,149
What about the man
that Angie said she was with,

966
00:58:11,251 --> 00:58:12,784
uh, Cole Reed?

967
00:58:12,886 --> 00:58:14,914
- Anything on him?
- Not on the company roster.

968
00:58:15,016 --> 00:58:16,822
But wait till you see this.

969
00:58:16,924 --> 00:58:18,389
[reporter on monitor]
<i>The suspect is very dangerous</i>

970
00:58:18,491 --> 00:58:20,087
<i>and still on the loose.</i>

971
00:58:20,190 --> 00:58:22,426
<i>A citywide order to shelter</i>
<i>is in place</i>

972
00:58:22,528 --> 00:58:24,857
<i>until he is apprehended.</i>

973
00:58:24,959 --> 00:58:26,964
A cop-killing fugitive.

974
00:58:27,765 --> 00:58:29,428
You have gotta be kidding me.

975
00:58:30,505 --> 00:58:32,706
Just what this shitshow
was missing.

976
00:58:34,301 --> 00:58:36,109
Get me satellite footage
of that ship.

977
00:58:36,211 --> 00:58:37,436
[Yates] Yes, sir.

978
00:58:38,278 --> 00:58:40,780
[metal creaking]

979
00:58:44,011 --> 00:58:45,216
[Angie grunts, strains]

980
00:58:45,318 --> 00:58:47,515
[wind whooshing]

981
00:58:47,617 --> 00:58:48,656
[Angie grunts]

982
00:58:55,361 --> 00:58:57,830
[action music]

983
00:59:02,335 --> 00:59:03,396
[Cole grunts]

984
00:59:07,870 --> 00:59:09,677
[Spencer] Well, shit.

985
00:59:11,137 --> 00:59:12,911
Tell me that's not an MP5.

986
00:59:14,312 --> 00:59:15,410
Sir.

987
00:59:16,013 --> 00:59:18,015
I hear there's a fugitive
on board.

988
00:59:18,750 --> 00:59:19,852
We know if he's a friendly?

989
00:59:21,057 --> 00:59:22,489
Friendly or not,

990
00:59:22,591 --> 00:59:24,282
make sure your men
are good to go.

991
00:59:24,384 --> 00:59:25,990
We launch
as soon as they're ready.

992
00:59:27,226 --> 00:59:28,190
Sir.

993
00:59:32,565 --> 00:59:33,934
[action music continues]

994
00:59:34,037 --> 00:59:34,999
[strains]

995
00:59:42,943 --> 00:59:44,943
[crewman] I think
I heard something over here.

996
00:59:46,847 --> 00:59:49,441
- Over there!
- Cole, someone's coming.

997
00:59:49,543 --> 00:59:51,744
- [metal creaking]
- [flashlight button clicks]

998
00:59:51,846 --> 00:59:54,084
[tense music]

999
00:59:58,857 --> 01:00:01,696
- [gunshots]
- [bullets ricocheting]

1000
01:00:02,762 --> 01:00:05,227
- [scraping]
- Shit! [grunting]

1001
01:00:10,568 --> 01:00:13,037
[panting]

1002
01:00:16,574 --> 01:00:19,439
[wind whooshing]

1003
01:00:25,880 --> 01:00:27,986
[metal creaking]

1004
01:00:29,886 --> 01:00:31,418
[Cole breathing heavily]

1005
01:00:52,775 --> 01:00:53,781
[metal creaks]

1006
01:00:55,141 --> 01:00:57,414
[breathing heavily]

1007
01:00:57,516 --> 01:00:58,746
[thuds lightly]

1008
01:00:58,848 --> 01:01:00,480
[clanging echoes]

1009
01:01:02,191 --> 01:01:05,654
[gunshots]

1010
01:01:05,756 --> 01:01:08,425
[scraping, creaking]

1011
01:01:08,527 --> 01:01:09,522
[muffled thud]

1012
01:01:11,464 --> 01:01:13,364
[metal groaning]

1013
01:01:13,466 --> 01:01:14,703
[cover clatters]

1014
01:01:28,613 --> 01:01:29,817
[Angie grunts]

1015
01:01:31,484 --> 01:01:32,545
Now, we're even.

1016
01:01:36,651 --> 01:01:38,219
[crewman over radio]
<i>Captain, we shot the stowaway</i>

1017
01:01:38,321 --> 01:01:40,085
<i>through the vent shaft,</i>
<i>heard him drop.</i>

1018
01:01:40,187 --> 01:01:41,394
Don't know if we hit him.

1019
01:01:41,496 --> 01:01:42,526
[Marko]<i> Block the hole.</i>

1020
01:01:42,628 --> 01:01:44,092
<i>Return to deck.</i>

1021
01:01:44,194 --> 01:01:46,429
<i>I'll take care</i>
<i>of this guy myself.</i>

1022
01:01:46,531 --> 01:01:47,494
Copy.

1023
01:01:49,362 --> 01:01:51,402
[Angie exhales sharply] Fuck.

1024
01:01:51,504 --> 01:01:52,741
[glass crunches]

1025
01:01:54,241 --> 01:01:55,337
Oh.

1026
01:01:58,712 --> 01:02:00,375
I'd like to see you twirl now.

1027
01:02:01,217 --> 01:02:02,344
Sit down.

1028
01:02:04,354 --> 01:02:05,817
The four of you, with me.

1029
01:02:05,919 --> 01:02:08,783
- Everybody else, fan out.
- [crunches]

1030
01:02:09,318 --> 01:02:10,950
- You keep an eye on her.
- Yes, sir.

1031
01:02:11,052 --> 01:02:12,722
[Marko] Let's go.

1032
01:02:12,824 --> 01:02:14,087
[Spencer] How far are we?

1033
01:02:14,189 --> 01:02:15,227
[Turner] Forty-two miles, sir.

1034
01:02:15,329 --> 01:02:16,264
Time?

1035
01:02:16,366 --> 01:02:17,931
Seventy-five minutes, sir.

1036
01:02:18,731 --> 01:02:19,825
Launch the VBSS crew.

1037
01:02:19,928 --> 01:02:21,102
Yes, sir.

1038
01:02:21,204 --> 01:02:24,036
[action music]

1039
01:02:27,441 --> 01:02:28,436
[hatch opens]

1040
01:02:29,102 --> 01:02:31,703
[engine revving]

1041
01:02:51,060 --> 01:02:52,595
[action music continues]

1042
01:02:52,697 --> 01:02:54,968
[engine revving]

1043
01:03:17,052 --> 01:03:18,960
[exhales sharply]

1044
01:03:19,729 --> 01:03:22,823
- [gunshot]
- [electricity crackling]

1045
01:03:22,925 --> 01:03:27,396
[alarm blaring]

1046
01:03:29,802 --> 01:03:31,668
[alarm continues blaring]

1047
01:03:31,770 --> 01:03:34,238
[suspenseful music]

1048
01:03:34,937 --> 01:03:36,075
[inhales]

1049
01:03:57,324 --> 01:04:01,864
[alarm blaring faintly]

1050
01:04:01,966 --> 01:04:06,336
[blaring intensifies]

1051
01:04:09,337 --> 01:04:11,212
- [squeaks]
- [lock clicks]

1052
01:04:11,314 --> 01:04:12,510
[exhales loudly]

1053
01:04:12,612 --> 01:04:13,876
He's trapped.

1054
01:04:13,978 --> 01:04:15,279
We'll deal with him later.

1055
01:04:16,012 --> 01:04:17,209
Captain to bridge.

1056
01:04:17,945 --> 01:04:20,284
- Lock off cargo hold three.
- [crewman over radio]<i> Sir.</i>

1057
01:04:25,893 --> 01:04:28,655
- [metal groaning]
- [straining]

1058
01:04:33,165 --> 01:04:35,497
- [groaning continues]
- [straining]

1059
01:04:36,362 --> 01:04:39,732
[groaning continues]

1060
01:04:44,071 --> 01:04:45,243
[thud]

1061
01:04:46,910 --> 01:04:50,578
[clattering]

1062
01:04:52,751 --> 01:04:55,651
[clanging]

1063
01:04:55,753 --> 01:04:56,885
[grunts]

1064
01:04:56,987 --> 01:05:00,585
[thudding, clanging]

1065
01:05:00,687 --> 01:05:02,560
Got the intel package
on Cole Reed.

1066
01:05:02,662 --> 01:05:03,723
That'll be all.

1067
01:05:06,002 --> 01:05:08,426
[Underwood] Cole Reed,
born and raised in London.

1068
01:05:08,528 --> 01:05:10,068
Mom passed when he was seven.

1069
01:05:10,170 --> 01:05:12,235
Father was a cop.
Grandfather was a cop.

1070
01:05:12,337 --> 01:05:14,574
Finishes school,
goes right into the navy.

1071
01:05:14,676 --> 01:05:15,905
Royal Marines Commando.

1072
01:05:16,007 --> 01:05:17,744
Two tours in Afghanistan.

1073
01:05:17,846 --> 01:05:20,312
Comes home,
joins the London police.

1074
01:05:20,414 --> 01:05:23,641
<i>Police Combat Cross for acts</i>
<i>of extraordinary heroism</i>

1075
01:05:23,743 --> 01:05:25,244
<i>while engaged</i>
<i>in personal combat</i>

1076
01:05:25,346 --> 01:05:26,818
<i>with an armed adversary.</i>

1077
01:05:26,920 --> 01:05:28,480
Meritorious Police Duty Award

1078
01:05:28,582 --> 01:05:30,319
for an act
of extraordinary bravery

1079
01:05:30,421 --> 01:05:32,752
intelligently performed
in the line of duty.

1080
01:05:35,358 --> 01:05:37,131
<i>Ends up serving under his dad</i>

1081
01:05:37,233 --> 01:05:40,697
<i>in the high-speed SCO19</i>
<i>Specialist Firearms Command.</i>

1082
01:05:41,266 --> 01:05:43,101
His unit was stalking
a mob operation.

1083
01:05:43,203 --> 01:05:45,367
On the takedown night,
Reed went too far,

1084
01:05:45,470 --> 01:05:47,939
disobeyed orders,
got himself stuck inside.

1085
01:05:48,408 --> 01:05:51,474
His father went in to save him
and was shot and killed.

1086
01:05:52,206 --> 01:05:53,206
Wait a second.

1087
01:05:53,308 --> 01:05:54,447
His father was killed

1088
01:05:54,549 --> 01:05:55,549
saving him?

1089
01:05:55,651 --> 01:05:56,809
[Underwood] Yes, sir.

1090
01:05:57,585 --> 01:05:58,712
[Spencer] Jesus.

1091
01:06:00,580 --> 01:06:02,656
<i>So, why'd he leave the UK?</i>

1092
01:06:02,758 --> 01:06:04,220
[Underwood]<i> File goes cold.</i>

1093
01:06:04,322 --> 01:06:05,826
<i>A lot of people looking</i>
<i>for payback,</i>

1094
01:06:05,928 --> 01:06:08,826
and, well...
he has no family left.

1095
01:06:08,928 --> 01:06:11,230
[Spencer breathes deeply]

1096
01:06:12,396 --> 01:06:15,904
I'll bet my pension
and my '67 Shelby

1097
01:06:16,006 --> 01:06:18,435
that whoever killed Campallo
is on that boat...

1098
01:06:19,767 --> 01:06:22,002
and Cole Reed is there
to square things up.

1099
01:06:22,104 --> 01:06:24,342
[tense music]

1100
01:06:30,916 --> 01:06:35,452
[singing in Thai]

1101
01:06:40,860 --> 01:06:43,398
[breathes heavily]

1102
01:06:43,500 --> 01:06:46,265
[breathes sharply]

1103
01:06:57,273 --> 01:07:01,643
[metal squeaks, creaking]

1104
01:07:02,518 --> 01:07:03,678
[gasps softly]

1105
01:07:06,479 --> 01:07:10,190
[ship horn blaring]

1106
01:07:15,125 --> 01:07:18,495
[ship horn blaring]

1107
01:07:32,749 --> 01:07:35,314
- [thudding]
- [sniffles]

1108
01:07:47,158 --> 01:07:48,493
[Marko] Lower the gangway.

1109
01:07:49,262 --> 01:07:50,560
- Lowering gangway.
- [button clicks]

1110
01:07:51,160 --> 01:07:53,761
[whirring]

1111
01:08:00,543 --> 01:08:02,671
[metal groaning]

1112
01:08:07,583 --> 01:08:09,678
[squeaks]

1113
01:08:13,283 --> 01:08:15,849
[phone ringtone playing]

1114
01:08:19,090 --> 01:08:20,293
Did the funds hit?

1115
01:08:25,700 --> 01:08:27,492
Funds confirmed.

1116
01:08:27,594 --> 01:08:29,929
What about our problem?

1117
01:08:31,773 --> 01:08:33,273
It's been contained.

1118
01:08:39,211 --> 01:08:40,709
Let's go and meet our guests.

1119
01:08:42,718 --> 01:08:45,714
[intriguing music]

1120
01:08:58,394 --> 01:08:59,596
Take them to the cargo.

1121
01:09:02,400 --> 01:09:04,738
- Ah, Cap.
- [Marko] Bertus.

1122
01:09:04,840 --> 01:09:06,234
[Bertus] Let's do it.

1123
01:09:06,803 --> 01:09:09,177
I saw smoke coming
from your ship on the way in.

1124
01:09:10,514 --> 01:09:11,845
Oh, yeah?

1125
01:09:11,947 --> 01:09:12,911
Well, what happens on my ship

1126
01:09:13,013 --> 01:09:14,043
is none of your business.

1127
01:09:14,145 --> 01:09:15,183
[Bertus chuckles]

1128
01:09:17,845 --> 01:09:19,985
- You wanna do this or what?
- Yeah.

1129
01:09:20,087 --> 01:09:21,453
Let's go inspect the goods.

1130
01:09:22,993 --> 01:09:24,786
I need to find myself
a clean one.

1131
01:09:25,854 --> 01:09:27,921
Best part of this job
is the ride home.

1132
01:09:28,864 --> 01:09:31,190
- Get in.
- [woman yelps]

1133
01:09:31,292 --> 01:09:32,299
Move.

1134
01:09:35,838 --> 01:09:36,963
[crewman] Get in there.

1135
01:09:47,542 --> 01:09:50,441
[thudding, clattering]

1136
01:09:50,543 --> 01:09:51,648
Thank you, Tibu.

1137
01:09:54,283 --> 01:09:56,950
[straining]

1138
01:10:00,189 --> 01:10:01,625
[sighs]

1139
01:10:02,456 --> 01:10:04,397
[metal creaking]

1140
01:10:05,162 --> 01:10:08,335
[action music]

1141
01:10:21,047 --> 01:10:23,350
[engine rumbling]

1142
01:10:25,413 --> 01:10:27,717
[grunting]

1143
01:10:43,564 --> 01:10:46,098
[light bulb buzzing]

1144
01:10:56,676 --> 01:10:58,946
[suspenseful music]

1145
01:11:04,694 --> 01:11:07,119
[ominous music]

1146
01:11:09,260 --> 01:11:12,267
[breathing sharply]

1147
01:11:16,464 --> 01:11:18,666
[grunting]

1148
01:11:18,768 --> 01:11:21,601
- Aah! [grunting]
- [strap creaking]

1149
01:11:21,703 --> 01:11:22,940
- [Cole grunts]
- [body thuds]

1150
01:11:23,042 --> 01:11:25,907
[intense music]

1151
01:11:31,380 --> 01:11:32,320
[Angie grunts]

1152
01:11:37,585 --> 01:11:38,659
[woman whimpering]

1153
01:11:38,761 --> 01:11:39,789
Here they are.

1154
01:11:41,887 --> 01:11:43,496
Now, get 'em off my ship.

1155
01:11:45,497 --> 01:11:46,799
- [crewmen grunt]
- [body thuds]

1156
01:11:46,901 --> 01:11:47,992
[gun cocks]

1157
01:11:48,094 --> 01:11:49,298
[Bertus]
What the fuck is going on?

1158
01:11:49,400 --> 01:11:51,306
[migrants gasp, whimper]

1159
01:11:56,109 --> 01:11:57,444
We have a stowaway.

1160
01:11:58,275 --> 01:11:59,580
A stowaway?

1161
01:11:59,682 --> 01:12:00,680
Yeah.

1162
01:12:01,149 --> 01:12:02,411
Well, what happens on your ship

1163
01:12:02,513 --> 01:12:04,244
is my fucking business now.

1164
01:12:04,347 --> 01:12:05,414
Calm down.

1165
01:12:05,516 --> 01:12:08,251
Everybody, calm down. Okay?

1166
01:12:08,353 --> 01:12:10,325
I will fix it. Calm down.

1167
01:12:12,251 --> 01:12:15,993
Boys, go down
and take care of this guy. Now.

1168
01:12:16,095 --> 01:12:17,596
Go! Go, go, go!

1169
01:12:19,331 --> 01:12:21,025
Mateo, go to the bridge

1170
01:12:21,127 --> 01:12:23,070
and deal with that bitch
once and for all.

1171
01:12:23,172 --> 01:12:24,867
- You understand?
- Yes, sir.

1172
01:12:27,171 --> 01:12:28,533
[clunks]

1173
01:12:28,635 --> 01:12:30,169
[door groaning]

1174
01:12:31,606 --> 01:12:33,942
[breathing sharply]

1175
01:12:35,444 --> 01:12:36,782
[door groans]

1176
01:12:36,884 --> 01:12:37,847
[gasps]

1177
01:12:44,787 --> 01:12:46,961
- [crewman grunting]
- [gunshots]

1178
01:12:47,063 --> 01:12:48,363
- [blood spurts]
- [body thuds]

1179
01:12:49,227 --> 01:12:51,894
[tense music]

1180
01:13:04,913 --> 01:13:06,579
[Angie grunts]

1181
01:13:09,414 --> 01:13:10,913
[indistinct radio chatter]

1182
01:13:12,580 --> 01:13:14,122
[crunches]

1183
01:13:14,224 --> 01:13:17,324
[crewman yelling,
grunts in pain]

1184
01:13:17,427 --> 01:13:20,593
- [crewman groans, grunts]
- [glass crackles]

1185
01:13:23,327 --> 01:13:25,928
[panting]

1186
01:13:27,035 --> 01:13:29,734
[running footsteps]

1187
01:13:30,668 --> 01:13:31,936
- [Mateo] Aah!
- [body thuds]

1188
01:13:32,038 --> 01:13:33,002
Fucker.

1189
01:13:33,437 --> 01:13:35,740
[breathing heavily]

1190
01:13:38,773 --> 01:13:41,108
[tense music continues]

1191
01:13:53,720 --> 01:13:57,631
[grunting]

1192
01:13:57,733 --> 01:13:58,622
Aah!

1193
01:13:58,725 --> 01:14:01,301
[grunting]

1194
01:14:01,403 --> 01:14:04,637
- [Cole grunting]
- [crewman 1 groans]

1195
01:14:05,907 --> 01:14:06,797
[grunts]

1196
01:14:06,899 --> 01:14:08,399
[crewman 2 grunting]

1197
01:14:10,142 --> 01:14:11,204
[grunts]

1198
01:14:12,144 --> 01:14:13,107
[grunts]

1199
01:14:14,312 --> 01:14:15,274
[body thuds]

1200
01:14:17,448 --> 01:14:18,409
[whispering] Shh.

1201
01:14:19,417 --> 01:14:20,513
Go to the stairs.

1202
01:14:20,615 --> 01:14:21,984
I'll go. Yeah?

1203
01:14:36,269 --> 01:14:39,430
[suspenseful music]

1204
01:14:40,233 --> 01:14:42,235
- [exhales sharply]
- [door creaks]

1205
01:14:43,737 --> 01:14:46,008
[grunting]

1206
01:14:47,807 --> 01:14:49,682
[grunting]

1207
01:14:50,285 --> 01:14:51,345
- [bones snap]
- [grunts]

1208
01:14:51,447 --> 01:14:52,619
[grunts]

1209
01:14:55,155 --> 01:14:58,185
[tense music]

1210
01:15:06,496 --> 01:15:08,360
[knife clatters]

1211
01:15:10,701 --> 01:15:13,431
- [gunshots]
- [panting]

1212
01:15:15,835 --> 01:15:17,270
[gun clicks]

1213
01:15:26,780 --> 01:15:28,050
[door groans]

1214
01:15:31,655 --> 01:15:34,056
[tense music intensifies]

1215
01:15:34,854 --> 01:15:35,827
[gunshots]

1216
01:15:42,499 --> 01:15:43,901
[gunshots]

1217
01:15:45,304 --> 01:15:46,970
[gun clicks]

1218
01:15:48,703 --> 01:15:52,605
[both grunting]

1219
01:15:52,707 --> 01:15:54,213
[yells, grunts]

1220
01:15:54,315 --> 01:15:55,709
[Cole exhales sharply]

1221
01:15:55,811 --> 01:15:59,153
[both grunting, straining]

1222
01:15:59,255 --> 01:16:01,552
- [kick lands]
- [grunting]

1223
01:16:01,654 --> 01:16:04,757
- [both grunting]
- [Marko] Ah!

1224
01:16:06,020 --> 01:16:08,822
[Cole yells, grunting in pain]

1225
01:16:08,924 --> 01:16:10,565
- [Marko grunts]
- [Cole yells]

1226
01:16:12,661 --> 01:16:15,097
[Cole straining]

1227
01:16:18,908 --> 01:16:20,271
[grunts]

1228
01:16:20,373 --> 01:16:23,039
[foreboding music]

1229
01:16:32,922 --> 01:16:33,918
[grunts]

1230
01:16:37,457 --> 01:16:39,858
[Marko] Ahh! [grunts]

1231
01:16:40,458 --> 01:16:43,455
[metal groaning]

1232
01:16:47,299 --> 01:16:48,262
[grunts]

1233
01:16:49,533 --> 01:16:52,171
[grunting]

1234
01:16:52,273 --> 01:16:55,999
[grunting continues]

1235
01:16:56,101 --> 01:16:58,869
[yelling, grunting]

1236
01:16:58,971 --> 01:17:00,310
[Marko] Ahh!

1237
01:17:00,412 --> 01:17:03,277
[loud clanging]

1238
01:17:06,616 --> 01:17:07,985
[Marko grunts]

1239
01:17:14,063 --> 01:17:16,730
[straining]

1240
01:17:20,261 --> 01:17:23,297
- [grunts]
- [Marko yelling in pain]

1241
01:17:25,167 --> 01:17:28,175
- [Cole yells]
- [Marko grunts, groans]

1242
01:17:28,277 --> 01:17:31,542
[Cole grunts, coughs]

1243
01:17:31,644 --> 01:17:36,016
[breathing heavily, grunts]

1244
01:17:36,118 --> 01:17:37,817
[Marko grunts]

1245
01:17:42,783 --> 01:17:43,955
[growls]

1246
01:17:48,859 --> 01:17:50,755
You should have died in Bangkok.

1247
01:17:51,491 --> 01:17:53,066
- [hook pierces flesh]
- [Marko yells in pain]

1248
01:17:53,168 --> 01:17:55,368
[both grunting]

1249
01:17:55,470 --> 01:17:57,528
[Marko yells, grunts in pain]

1250
01:17:57,630 --> 01:18:00,339
- [Cole grunting]
- [Marko grunts, yells in pain]

1251
01:18:00,441 --> 01:18:05,504
Aah! [panting, grunting]

1252
01:18:07,142 --> 01:18:09,647
- [Marko growls] Aah!
- [grunts]

1253
01:18:09,749 --> 01:18:12,076
- [grunts]
- [yelling in pain]

1254
01:18:12,178 --> 01:18:14,788
[Marko grunting in pain]

1255
01:18:18,050 --> 01:18:19,023
[grunts in pain]

1256
01:18:19,888 --> 01:18:22,620
[yelling in pain]

1257
01:18:23,460 --> 01:18:24,791
Ah!

1258
01:18:24,893 --> 01:18:26,327
This is for Tibu.

1259
01:18:38,643 --> 01:18:39,714
[spear gun thuds]

1260
01:18:45,813 --> 01:18:46,812
[sighs]

1261
01:18:46,914 --> 01:18:49,383
[dramatic music]

1262
01:18:56,088 --> 01:18:59,063
[bird squawking]

1263
01:19:04,329 --> 01:19:07,236
[bird continues squawking]

1264
01:19:17,276 --> 01:19:20,183
[dramatic music continues]

1265
01:19:29,432 --> 01:19:31,029
[Tully] Stay the fuck down.

1266
01:19:34,533 --> 01:19:35,902
Just stay down.

1267
01:19:37,439 --> 01:19:40,366
Don't you fucking move.

1268
01:19:40,469 --> 01:19:42,304
- Get the cuffs on him.
- [Navy Seal] Yes, sir.

1269
01:19:46,446 --> 01:19:47,606
[Angie] Wait!

1270
01:19:49,582 --> 01:19:50,547
[Navy Seal] Move it.

1271
01:19:50,649 --> 01:19:52,680
[running footsteps]

1272
01:19:52,782 --> 01:19:53,744
[Angie grunts]

1273
01:20:00,055 --> 01:20:01,193
[Angie] I'm not armed.

1274
01:20:01,896 --> 01:20:04,187
- Who are you?
- I'm Angie Ellis. I called you.

1275
01:20:04,289 --> 01:20:05,723
I'm the third mate.

1276
01:20:06,832 --> 01:20:08,165
He has nothing to do with this.

1277
01:20:08,732 --> 01:20:10,130
He saved us.

1278
01:20:10,232 --> 01:20:11,630
[Tully] Where's the rest
of the crew?

1279
01:20:13,002 --> 01:20:14,001
[Angie] They're dead.

1280
01:20:14,103 --> 01:20:15,972
[Tully] How many were there?

1281
01:20:16,074 --> 01:20:19,242
[Angie] About 20.
And the captain.

1282
01:20:21,779 --> 01:20:22,983
Is that Cole Reed?

1283
01:20:23,085 --> 01:20:24,247
No.

1284
01:20:25,112 --> 01:20:26,249
That's my shipmate.

1285
01:20:29,825 --> 01:20:33,322
You're telling us
that that isn't Cole?

1286
01:20:34,256 --> 01:20:36,523
Cole was shot.
He went overboard.

1287
01:20:37,924 --> 01:20:38,965
Ah.

1288
01:20:41,166 --> 01:20:43,527
- So that's how it went down?
- [inhales]

1289
01:20:43,629 --> 01:20:47,171
Yeah, that's how
it went down, sir.

1290
01:20:50,139 --> 01:20:51,637
[Tully] Keep an eye on her.

1291
01:20:53,216 --> 01:20:54,178
[exhales]

1292
01:20:55,648 --> 01:20:56,708
[Tully] Get him up.

1293
01:20:59,379 --> 01:21:01,152
Looks like you had a rough day.

1294
01:21:02,886 --> 01:21:04,114
Let's check you out.

1295
01:21:05,017 --> 01:21:07,686
There are people on that ship
that need medical attention.

1296
01:21:11,732 --> 01:21:13,868
- All right?
- Oh, yeah.

1297
01:21:16,572 --> 01:21:18,169
[Angie] Yes, that's correct.

1298
01:21:19,300 --> 01:21:21,502
I'll be waiting. Thank you.

1299
01:21:25,209 --> 01:21:26,545
They're sending me a crew
to help me

1300
01:21:26,647 --> 01:21:28,047
with the route back to LA.

1301
01:21:29,181 --> 01:21:30,909
[smacks lips]
So it's Captain Ellis now.

1302
01:21:31,011 --> 01:21:31,978
[laughs]

1303
01:21:32,080 --> 01:21:33,445
[Seng speaks Thai]

1304
01:21:33,547 --> 01:21:35,351
[Angie in English]
Yeah, I don't think so.

1305
01:21:36,384 --> 01:21:38,455
Is that Captain Marko's
sat phone?

1306
01:21:38,557 --> 01:21:40,252
It is.

1307
01:21:40,354 --> 01:21:41,788
Does it have a call log on it?

1308
01:21:41,891 --> 01:21:42,996
Of course.

1309
01:21:46,867 --> 01:21:48,595
- [Angie chuckles]
- Thank you.

1310
01:21:52,275 --> 01:21:53,336
Thank you.

1311
01:21:57,336 --> 01:22:00,409
[indistinct chatter]

1312
01:22:02,015 --> 01:22:03,412
[Angie]
So, where will you go now?

1313
01:22:04,245 --> 01:22:05,951
If you go back to Bangkok,

1314
01:22:06,053 --> 01:22:07,922
you know that they're gonna try
and kill you.

1315
01:22:09,624 --> 01:22:11,057
I need to finish this.

1316
01:22:15,695 --> 01:22:16,964
Get home to Violet.

1317
01:22:19,293 --> 01:22:20,858
[chuckles softly] I will.

1318
01:22:24,572 --> 01:22:26,196
[gasps softly] Ah.

1319
01:22:26,298 --> 01:22:29,570
[soft music]

1320
01:22:38,413 --> 01:22:40,012
[Spencer]
<i>Is the Artemis secured?</i>

1321
01:22:40,581 --> 01:22:42,584
[Tully]<i> Yes, sir.</i>
<i>Artemis secure.</i>

1322
01:22:43,154 --> 01:22:45,151
[Spencer]<i> Is Cole Reed secured?</i>

1323
01:22:45,754 --> 01:22:48,954
According to Miss Ellis,
Reed was killed in action, sir.

1324
01:22:49,590 --> 01:22:52,222
Marko and all 20
of his crew killed.

1325
01:22:52,324 --> 01:22:53,966
Twenty killed?

1326
01:22:54,068 --> 01:22:55,226
[Tully over sat phone]
<i>Twenty-one, sir.</i>

1327
01:22:55,328 --> 01:22:56,399
<i>Plus the pirates.</i>

1328
01:22:57,633 --> 01:23:00,898
There was one friendly crewman
we didn't identify

1329
01:23:01,000 --> 01:23:04,737
who appears to be taking off
on the pirate boat, sir.

1330
01:23:06,808 --> 01:23:08,613
[Spencer]<i> Wait a second.</i>
<i>Let me get this straight.</i>

1331
01:23:09,249 --> 01:23:12,182
Cole Reed is KIA,
but you do not have a body,

1332
01:23:12,284 --> 01:23:14,478
and now, there's
this unidentified crewman

1333
01:23:14,580 --> 01:23:16,985
heading off on a pirate ship.

1334
01:23:17,087 --> 01:23:18,586
<i>Do I have that correct?</i>

1335
01:23:19,686 --> 01:23:21,292
[Tully]
<i>Yes, sir, that's correct.</i>

1336
01:23:22,929 --> 01:23:24,526
<i>You want us to intercept?</i>

1337
01:23:26,135 --> 01:23:29,795
Well, since he is not Cole Reed,
he is not our problem.

1338
01:23:31,540 --> 01:23:33,164
I would agree, sir.

1339
01:23:33,266 --> 01:23:36,505
[tense music]

1340
01:23:37,172 --> 01:23:41,444
[cell phone ringing]

1341
01:23:44,016 --> 01:23:45,079
[Cole over phone]<i> It's me.</i>

1342
01:23:45,181 --> 01:23:46,285
Jesus. Where are you?

1343
01:23:46,821 --> 01:23:48,519
I need you to run a number.

1344
01:23:48,621 --> 01:23:49,650
One sec.

1345
01:23:54,291 --> 01:23:55,395
- [keyboard clacks]
- Go on.

1346
01:23:55,497 --> 01:23:59,891
667-213-4777.

1347
01:24:02,132 --> 01:24:03,697
[Taran] Jaran Daniles.

1348
01:24:04,836 --> 01:24:05,897
I'm coming back.

1349
01:24:06,773 --> 01:24:07,833
[sat phone beeps]

1350
01:24:08,567 --> 01:24:11,408
[tense music continues]

1351
01:24:20,987 --> 01:24:22,780
[woman] Such a lovely service.

1352
01:24:22,883 --> 01:24:25,552
I thought everyone did
such a beautiful job.

1353
01:24:25,654 --> 01:24:28,260
[man] The community
will miss him so much.

1354
01:24:30,357 --> 01:24:33,265
[foreboding music]

1355
01:24:36,867 --> 01:24:37,830
Get in.

1356
01:24:41,335 --> 01:24:42,340
[car door closes]

1357
01:24:49,443 --> 01:24:52,185
[Cole breathes deeply]

1358
01:24:55,416 --> 01:24:56,585
You don't understand.

1359
01:24:58,689 --> 01:25:00,956
I just let them use the ships
to transport cargo,

1360
01:25:01,058 --> 01:25:02,261
and they paid me.

1361
01:25:03,126 --> 01:25:04,395
They paid me a lot.

1362
01:25:06,565 --> 01:25:10,197
But I had no idea what they were
really asking me to do.

1363
01:25:10,299 --> 01:25:11,765
You have to believe me.

1364
01:25:13,870 --> 01:25:16,638
And then they stopped asking
and they started threatening.

1365
01:25:17,771 --> 01:25:19,476
And that's when things
got out of hand.

1366
01:25:21,245 --> 01:25:23,711
Multiple shipments every week.

1367
01:25:26,216 --> 01:25:27,954
Why didn't you come to me?

1368
01:25:28,056 --> 01:25:30,322
Because I thought
I had it handled.

1369
01:25:33,327 --> 01:25:35,591
I thought selling the company
would get me out.

1370
01:25:38,097 --> 01:25:40,191
But I never knew that they...

1371
01:25:40,761 --> 01:25:42,433
I didn't think
they'd go this far.

1372
01:25:45,137 --> 01:25:46,739
You got your father killed.

1373
01:25:46,841 --> 01:25:49,099
[sighs, inhales sharply]

1374
01:25:51,509 --> 01:25:53,103
And you're gonna have to live
with that.

1375
01:25:54,409 --> 01:25:55,809
For the rest of your life.

1376
01:25:57,983 --> 01:25:59,483
[inhales shakily]

1377
01:26:04,584 --> 01:26:06,757
[sighs] Take him home.

1378
01:26:06,859 --> 01:26:08,327
[car door opens]

1379
01:26:10,193 --> 01:26:11,165
[car door closes]

1380
01:26:12,161 --> 01:26:15,202
[intense music]

1381
01:26:39,859 --> 01:26:41,492
[loud crash]

1382
01:26:46,229 --> 01:26:48,532
[metal squeaking]

1383
01:26:51,640 --> 01:26:53,636
[engine hisses]

1384
01:26:56,668 --> 01:26:57,838
[car door closes]

1385
01:26:59,671 --> 01:27:01,006
[Daniles groaning]

1386
01:27:06,314 --> 01:27:07,518
[Daniles gasps]

1387
01:27:09,681 --> 01:27:15,152
[grunting, panting]

1388
01:27:16,522 --> 01:27:17,891
Why kill Tibu?

1389
01:27:19,365 --> 01:27:22,134
Tibu dies,
the company goes to Kameron,

1390
01:27:22,236 --> 01:27:25,003
who's compromised,
who we control,

1391
01:27:25,105 --> 01:27:26,767
and our cargo business goes on.

1392
01:27:26,869 --> 01:27:29,100
You mean the human beings
you were trafficking?

1393
01:27:30,244 --> 01:27:32,911
What do you want?
[continues panting]

1394
01:27:33,013 --> 01:27:34,840
Everybody wants something.

1395
01:27:34,942 --> 01:27:37,845
Tell me what you want.
I'll get it for you.

1396
01:27:40,515 --> 01:27:42,179
What the fuck do you want?

1397
01:27:42,856 --> 01:27:44,687
[Daniles grunts]

1398
01:27:52,261 --> 01:27:53,465
Vengeance.

1399
01:27:54,131 --> 01:27:57,194
[intense music]

1400
01:29:34,199 --> 01:29:35,460
[music fades out]

1401
01:29:35,562 --> 01:29:38,229
[tense music]

1402
01:30:47,470 --> 01:30:48,941
[music fades out]

1403
01:30:49,043 --> 01:30:52,072
[unsettling music]

1404
01:31:50,665 --> 01:31:51,696
[music fades out]

1405
01:31:51,798 --> 01:31:54,838
[intriguing music]

1406
01:32:55,202 --> 01:32:57,032
[music fades out]

1407
01:32:59,106 --> 01:33:02,169
[soft music]

1408
01:33:58,991 --> 01:34:00,032
[music fades out]

1409
01:34:00,134 --> 01:34:03,164
[dramatic music]

1410
01:34:54,816 --> 01:34:56,723
[music fades out]

